{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/1792632000000-engineer-8ab-fix1.report.md collab/1792620000000-8ab-regen.clj collab/1792620000000-engineer-8ab.report.md'","aggregated_output":"Completed-GMT: 2026-10-14 16:43:50 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-14 23:43:50 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\nCoding-Agent: codex\nSession-ID: 01a13b4b-763f-7c10-8ef4-9b01b60d6976\n\nBlocked: the named worktree lacks the stated I4-a rebase dependencies. No pins were edited and no commit was made.\n\nRead the architecture rules, phase-8 plan §1.4, supplied regen script, Fable review, prior engineering report, and build/test guide before verification.\n\n## Dependency evidence\n\n- HEAD: `6e38c90f4647bc539cda375e665833e8e8ae2727`.\n- Local `origin/master`: `2c70bec18b0831080375db932b324d478f14918a`.\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor bcf5a3a8 HEAD`: exit 1. The artifact regen commit exists locally but is not in this tree's ancestry.\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor d09a557c HEAD`: exit 1. The I4-a statement-time import commit exists locally but is not in this tree's ancestry.\n- The artifact's latest commit in HEAD is `bdaed7ff`, the earlier regen, rather than `bcf5a3a8`.\n\nThe brief requires stopping before expanding dependency edits. Applying these missing commits would change files outside the named golden files, including the other seat's files. Authorization or a corrected rebased worktree is required before proceeding.\n\n## Completed checks\n\n| Check | Actual outcome |\n|---|---|\n| `clojure -M collab/1792620000000-8ab-regen.clj` | Exit 0; 51 entries recomputed, descriptor equality and exact handoff fixture byte assertions passed |\n| `cmp target/8ab/regen-2.edn target/8ab-fix1/regen.edn` | Exit 0; all 51 outputs byte-identical to the prior run |\n| Focused quick, nine prior touched namespaces plus `yin.vm.ucf.handoff-v2-census-test` | Exit 0; 250 tests, 8,483 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors |\n| `git diff --check` | Exit 0; clean |\n| `git diff --stat` | Empty; no tracked changes |\n\nQuick command:\n\n```sh\nclojure -M:test -e :slow -n yin.vm.debruijn-test -n yin.vm.debruijn-code-test -n yin.vm.debruijn-register-code-test -n yin.vm.debruijn-register-compile-test -n yin.vm.debruijn.stack-parity-test -n yin.vm.linker-test -n yin.vm.semantic-register.derive-test -n yang.python.antlr.linked-prelude-test -n yang.python.antlr.linked-safepoint-test -n yin.vm.ucf.handoff-v2-census-test\n```\n\nAn auxiliary live manifest probe used plain `-M` and failed with `FileNotFoundException` because the test harness is not on that classpath. It yielded no manifest evidence; no workaround or source edit followed. The actual quick command used `-M:test` and passed.\n\n## Pins and files\n\nNo pins moved; there are no old→new changes to report. The saved-input regen verified every previous H/R, descriptor, dimension/node, linker and handoff output unchanged. Its saved py/pysp manifest maps also produced the previous `577aabfb8632` / `6c39c4b94a08` addresses; these saved-input calculations do not constitute post-I4-a publication verification.\n\nAll tracked files remain byte-identical to starting HEAD, including backend, parity, corpus (32 pins), rows (20 pins), linker, both golden namespaces, and the two protected DHT import files. No CESK or execution-parity behavior changed. Existing untracked collab files were preserved.\n\nOnly this new report was written under collab. New ignored verification logs are under `target/8ab-fix1/` (`regen.edn`, `quick.log`, `live-manifests.log`). The report's Session-ID was captured from `CODEX_THREAD_ID`, which matches `CODEX_SESSION_ID`; a dispatch `thread.started` event is not exposed in this turn.\n\n## Incomplete work and concerns\n\nThe post-I4-a re-derivation is incomplete because the prerequisite tree is absent. Lint was not run (no code files changed); the slow `dht-import-test` leg and four mutants were not run after the dependency mismatch was established. Node/Dart were not run, as instructed; the orchestrator's reported results were not independently verified here. The two C4 namespaces' later host lanes remain the orchestrator's follow-up.\n\nPlease provide the corrected rebased worktree or authorize rebasing this branch onto the master revision containing `d09a557c` and `bcf5a3a8`. No edits to those dependencies will be made without that authorization.\n;; Run from the repository root: clojure -M collab/1792620000000-8ab-regen.clj\n;; The adjacent EDN file prints every intermediate; no lowerer or private var\n;; is needed. Projection fingerprints use printed map ASTs.\n(require '[clojure.edn :as edn]\n         '[clojure.string :as str]\n         '[dao.jing :as jing]\n         '[dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n         '[yin.vm :as vm]\n         '[yin.vm.debruijn :as db]\n         '[yin.vm.debruijn-code :as dc]\n         '[yin.vm.debruijn-register-code :as rcode])\n\n(def intermediates\n  (edn/read-string (slurp \"collab/1792620000000-8ab-intermediates.edn\")))\n\n(defn recompute [{:keys [kind input]}]\n  (case kind\n    :h (dc/image-hash input)\n    :r (rcode/register-hash input)\n    :descriptor (jing/blake3 (dc/encode-scalar input))\n    :dimension (jing/blake3 (db/encode-value input))\n    :projection (:fingerprint (db/project-datoms (vm/ast->datoms input)))\n    :segment (jing/segment-key input)))\n\n(assert (= dc/descriptor (get-in intermediates [\"44c761ee3ba9b5669385841b361b76f86f0b1db7b3b42f1c7966458669f6361e\" :input])))\n(assert (= rcode/descriptor\n           (get-in intermediates\n                   [\"7eacba41f9f1548d18b724cbd2db87945f09ec7b4ab2f303399e9b6497007632\" :input])))\n(assert (= db/descriptor\n           (get-in intermediates\n                   [\"1f4ec95cdfd666cf5da2be5f47fd3a7e3c942dfa2ea87e61e0062270f61a0803\" :input])))\n\n(doseq [[old entry] (sort-by key intermediates)]\n  (when (str/starts-with? old \"handoff-v2:\")\n    (let [[_ address & hex] (str/split-lines\n                             (slurp \"test/resources/yin/vm/ucf/handoff-v2.txt\"))\n          encoded (apply str (map #(format \"%02x\" (bit-and 255 %))\n                                  (cbor/encode (:input entry))))]\n      (assert (= address (subs (str (recompute entry)) 1)))\n      (assert (= (apply str hex) encoded))))\n  (prn [old (recompute entry)]))\n# Phase 8ab engineering report\n\nImplementation complete; verification results are recorded below. No commit was made.\n\n## Changes\n\nBoth backend descriptors drop `:dim/lift-to` and declare `:hash :blake3`.\nAll six surviving production hash sites use explicit `jing/blake3` on the\nportable hosts. `lowering-contract-version` remains 2; register\n`contract-version` remains 4. H and R are derived checksums; A is the sole\ncode identity. Descriptor comparisons against HEAD passed: exactly the\nlift-row removal and encoding `:hash` change, with no other data change.\n\nThe H descriptor golden now lives in the surviving `debruijn-code-test`.\nThe register descriptor golden remains in `debruijn-register-code-test`;\nits duplicated declaration/test was removed from the old compiler test.\nThe linker image helpers and stack-parity image producer use `derive`.\nThe stack parity test retains the old adapter only for the side-table\nassertion, which tests old lowerer behavior until 8e.\n\n`encode-scalar` needs no move: `yin.vm.debruijn-code` survives to compute H\nand supplies the register encoder. Its public function, descriptor reference\n`:yin.debruijn-code/encode-scalar`, and scalar tests remain valid. Neither\nbackend kernel was widened or removed.\n\n## Reproduction and every regenerated constant\n\nRun from the repository root:\n\n```sh\nclojure -M collab/1792620000000-8ab-regen.clj\n```\n\n[The script](./1792620000000-8ab-regen.clj) is 41 lines. Its\n[printed intermediates](./1792620000000-8ab-intermediates.edn) contain all\nimages, descriptors, ASTs and manifest maps. It uses only public functions;\nno old lowerer, private var, test namespace or network is needed. Projection\nroots are regenerated from their whole AST, so child hashes also regenerate.\nThe four literal-double fingerprints take the same public projection path\nas their tests. The H/R image bytes remain pinned in the tests.\n\nThe script also reconstructs and verifies the handoff fixture wire bytes.\nTwo final runs produced byte-identical stdout (`cmp`, exit 0), covering 51\nregeneration entries (50 distinct new values; the linker R now equals the\nnew lowerer's worked-example R). The H descriptor's old checksum was previously unpinned;\nits new checksum is pinned. Repeated occurrences of the worked-example H\n(derive, linker and parity) are one constant in this table. The register\nlinker golden has its own new `derive` image; the old compiler's checksum of\nits different allocation remains a separate entry.\n\nAliases below: `dc` = `yin.vm.debruijn-code`, `rcode` =\n`yin.vm.debruijn-register-code`, `db` = `yin.vm.debruijn`.\nEach input line refers to the companion EDN file. Prefixes have 12 hex digits.\n\n| Old prefix / role | New prefix | Recomputed with | Printed input line |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `1139b238ade4` | `336e197fed38` | `dc/image-hash` | 365 |\n| `188d78a7a966` | `cc4b808680b0` | `dc/image-hash` | 769 |\n| `1c4a5286b603` | `0d632c1df836` | `rcode/register-hash` | 350 |\n| `1f4ec95cdfd6` | `4b69e00d1da9` | `jing/blake3` of `db/encode-value` | 388 |\n| `2ba41668a217` | `6f64ba722c0e` | `dc/image-hash` | 373 |\n| `2f9d03004e23` | `4caa8d97945f` | `:fingerprint` of `db/project-datoms` on `vm/ast->datoms` | 499 |\n| `32d51cde25ba` | `0a1b29b833c6` | `dc/image-hash` | 34 |\n| `3d2f65270b0a` | `64afffdc1e88` | `dc/image-hash` | 193 |\n| `3eff0da5d025` | `415186d353a2` | `:fingerprint` of `db/project-datoms` on `vm/ast->datoms` | 45 |\n| `411b0a57a72c` | `6cae23688206` | `:fingerprint` of `db/project-datoms` on `vm/ast->datoms` | 65 |\n| `44c761ee3ba9` | `7b7c6ae92e5f` | `jing/blake3` of `dc/encode-scalar` | 517 |\n| `4dc65d3411d7` | `2e3a44ccf973` | `rcode/register-hash` | 716 |\n| `52791d4a2d0f` | `d07cb2e9a417` | `dc/image-hash` | 577 |\n| `52c71ac04f19` | `09e8c987e3b7` | `rcode/register-hash` | 786 |\n| `62198ed95487` | `babe1615ccf9` | `rcode/register-hash` | 47 |\n| `62ddeadc830b` | `fa643897ef8a` | `dc/image-hash` | 348 |\n| `64ebe1570b00` | `8713665b8a09` | `dc/image-hash` | 480 |\n| `685a0c512ae6` | `c75c61144769` | `rcode/register-hash` | 206 |\n| `6b8dea73d5a0` | `d748b428803c` | `dc/image-hash` | 478 |\n| `71926b1e251a` | `bc06914564a0` | `rcode/register-hash` | 501 |\n| `71aa237c3fd6` | `d078be3a34c1` | `rcode/register-hash` | 21 |\n| `728b09df940c` | `668cb6b1431b` | `rcode/register-hash` | 368 |\n| `74f3617eef6e` | `6f1105cee27b` | `rcode/register-hash` | 1650 |\n| `787f35c8ea6a` | `eaeda8e420db` | `rcode/register-hash` | 182 |\n| `7a97c0d6bed1` | `25b74c840986` | `rcode/register-hash` | 16 |\n| `7e5eeba449d1` | `d20861bf40f6` | `dc/image-hash` | 212 |\n| `7eacba41f9f1` | `aa757659a28f` | `jing/blake3` of `dc/encode-scalar` | 603 |\n| `8c80e1d1b1aa` | `83a461659f64` | `dc/image-hash` | 1 |\n| `8ea2568a409a` | `9762b17e54c3` | `rcode/register-hash` | 67 |\n| `91eee5759eec` | `87bc0840c109` | `rcode/register-hash` | 728 |\n| `9a4f2390af6d` | `7b2f6135e680` | `rcode/register-hash` | 483 |\n| `a71ffdee457d` | `172bc86cd013` | `dc/image-hash` | 757 |\n| `a9cfdb6d6cbc` | `87fda1b80fa1` | `rcode/register-hash` | 161 |\n| `aaa109a179b7` | `07de8d305555` | `rcode/register-hash` | 733 |\n| `add0178e7de1` | `1bf1ac57333e` | `dc/image-hash` | 1641 |\n| `aed64f20d715` | `25d418f9afbb` | `:fingerprint` of `db/project-datoms` on `vm/ast->datoms` | 196 |\n| `b3ee9e8c72e8` | `e0e8fdfca9d9` | `:fingerprint` of `db/project-datoms` on `vm/ast->datoms` | 32 |\n| `c0aefe2fa287` | `70de2f461733` | `rcode/register-hash` | 166 |\n| `e00c3b0d6325` | `9ab244f27567` | `dc/image-hash` | 784 |\n| `e780fb5067ce` | `decbf54ad753` | `rcode/register-hash` | 473 |\n| `e971cd9b084c` | `688b2b450aac` | `dc/image-hash` | 691 |\n| `eb70fa6d6b3a` | `f284fcb321a3` | `dc/image-hash` | 497 |\n| `f53e884408c9` | `e2fac210d293` | `rcode/register-hash` | 355 |\n| `f74e6e75631b` | `c4413a954f8a` | `dc/image-hash` | 594 |\n| `f86f480ae243` | `3c0622436b68` | `rcode/register-hash` | 56 |\n| `fb7626101d5e` | `236b6decefd5` | `rcode/register-hash` | 797 |\n| `fe79f9ab7e0a` | `f35503a87fbd` | `dc/image-hash` | 745 |\n| `handoff-v2:afe9e3ac1c3c` | `52c7efaa3967` | `jing/segment-key` | 227 |\n| `linker-R:c0aefe2fa287` | `bc06914564a0` | `rcode/register-hash` | 1655 |\n| `py:b9dbaeff80b3` | `577aabfb8632` | `jing/segment-key` | 813 |\n| `pysp:0971cc1ef48a` | `6c39c4b94a08` | `jing/segment-key` | 72 |\n\n## A-address gates\n\n`git diff --quiet` passed for `corpus.cljc` (32 pins), `rows_test.cljc`\n(20 pins), `layout_test.cljc`, the surviving safepoint harness, and the\n`rows-checkpoint-v3.txt` / `ledger-v2.txt` fixtures. They are byte-for-byte\nunchanged from HEAD. The broad VM suite exercises the corpus, rows, layout\nand harness gates. Python's prelude-independent program root is unchanged.\nNo A address or root pin was regenerated.\n\n## Verification\n\nAll final runs exited 0. Tests ran in foreground JVM processes; no commit,\nNode lane or Dart lane was run, as required by this brief. Logs are under\n`target/8ab/`.\n\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `clj -M:kondo --lint <changed Clojure files>` plus the whole `dao.jing` source/test family | 0 errors, 0 warnings |\n| Focused quick, `clojure -M:test -e :slow -n <each touched test namespace>` | 250 tests, 8,483 assertions, 0 failures/errors |\n| Focused slow, `clojure -M:test -i :slow -n <each touched test namespace>` | 17 tests, 200 assertions, 0 failures/errors |\n| Broad VM, command below | 1,149 tests, 25,237 assertions, 0 failures/errors |\n| `clojure -M:test -e :slow -r 'dao\\.jing.*'` | 233 tests, 10,383 assertions, 0 failures/errors; this family has no tagged slow tests |\n| Descriptor comparison against original HEAD forms | Exact two-row change for both descriptors; versions 2/4 unchanged |\n| Two final reproduction runs and `cmp` | Byte-identical output; exact handoff fixture bytes also verified |\n| `git diff --check` | Clean |\n\nBroad VM command:\n\n```sh\nclojure -M:test -e :slow -r 'yin\\.vm\\.(debruijn|semantic-register|linker|ucf)\\..*' -n yin.vm.pipeline-test\n```\n\nFocused namespaces: `yin.vm.debruijn-test`, `yin.vm.debruijn-code-test`,\n`yin.vm.debruijn-register-code-test`, `yin.vm.debruijn-register-compile-test`,\n`yin.vm.debruijn.stack-parity-test`, `yin.vm.linker-test`,\n`yin.vm.semantic-register.derive-test`,\n`yang.python.antlr.linked-prelude-test`, and\n`yang.python.antlr.linked-safepoint-test`. The final quick run additionally\nincludes `yin.vm.ucf.handoff-v2-census-test` for the changed fixture.\nThe C4 slow oracle completed 10 root programs and 8 module bodies across\nboth old/new backend families.\n\nThe first broad run could not load the absent generated Python parser.\n`clojure -M:antlr-gen` generated it after downloading the two checksum-pinned\nJava support files with network access. Sandboxed Jing/VM runs also failed\nthe real loopback socket tests; rerunning with approved local socket access\npassed. These environment failures were resolved without source changes.\nThe first broad run additionally exposed the stale handoff fixture, which\nwas regenerated before the final passing run.\n\n## Mutants\n\nEach mutant was applied alone after `cp` backup. Its diff was saved,\nits JVM test command exited 1 with the failures below, and the backup was\nrestored with `cp`. Restoration passed `git diff --no-index --quiet` against\nthe backup, and the before/after `git diff -- <file>` outputs were identical.\nThe real index was untouched. The final quick/broad suites passed after all\nfour restorations.\n\n| Mutant | Catching assertion / suite | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| H `image-hash` left on `jing/sha256` | `debruijn-code-test/golden-corpus-bytes-and-hash` | 4 failures, 0 errors |\n| Register descriptor `:hash` row left `:sha256` | `debruijn-register-code-test/golden-descriptor-hash-test` | 1 failure, 0 errors |\n| `:const-long` H pin regenerated using SHA-256 over the **current** descriptor hash and image encoding | `debruijn-code-test/golden-corpus-bytes-and-hash` | 1 failure, 0 errors |\n| Old worked-example H `52791d4a…` retained in the new lowerer's golden | `semantic-register.derive-test/stack-goldens` | 1 failure, 0 errors |\n\nAll four mutants were caught. Wrong-algorithm mutant value was computed with\n`(jing/sha256 (str dc/descriptor-hash (dc/encode-image [[:const 42] [:return]])))`,\nthen placed in the pin; it was not invented.\n\n\n## Deviations and design findings\n\n- The plan says 11 pins in `derive_test`; the code has 10 H plus 10 R pins.\n  All 20 were regenerated. `debruijn_code_test` has four additional H\n  goldens omitted from the inventory; all four were regenerated. Stack\n  parity has four distinct image/H rows and four wire-byte pins, rather\n  than the plan's six hashes/two hex images. Every wire-byte pin stayed.\n- The old register compiler test still exists until 8e. It has 11 image\n  checksum pins, not 12. Removing only its duplicated descriptor golden\n  while leaving stale checksum pins makes this slice fail. Those 11 pins\n  were regenerated from their printed images, preserving all image and\n  execution assertions until the planned deletion. No shim was added.\n- Production's named-root pairing verifier still uses the old register\n  allocator until 8c. Its authentic-pairing test explicitly produces the\n  old allocation locally; general linker helpers use `derive` as requested.\n  Switching production here would silently import an 8c semantic change.\n- `py` and `pysp` manifest addresses already change in 8ab because their\n  derivation outputs and checksum-keyed indexes embed H/R. Both were\n  regenerated now, with printed complete manifest maps. Their contract/map\n  shape and production pipeline remain current; 8c necessarily regenerates\n  these manifests again when that pipeline and manifest shape change. The\n  plan's claim that manifests move only once in the whole phase does not\n  match this intermediate slice dependency.\n- The registry/classification documents had stale claims that the register\n  implementation was absent and that four SHA-256 sites were current.\n  They now describe the six implemented BLAKE3 sites. Historical H0/H1\n  no-change obligations remain historical; SHA-256 remains an explicit,\n  permanent Jing registry member and the DHT routing contract stays SHA-256.\n- The broad suite found `handoff-v2.txt` embeds an H checksum in its CBOR\n  payload, despite the plan's claim that old transport fixtures contain no\n  H/R. Its plain hex does not expose the ASCII digest to a raw hash grep.\n  The fixture's image H and checkpoint address were regenerated using the\n  printed image and decoded body. The decoded body differs only by replacing\n  the embedded H throughout; its version, code rows, floats and cursor IDs remain identical; layout\n  structure is unchanged and its H references regenerate with that checksum. The reproduction script also verifies exact\n  fixture bytes. The fixture stays until its planned 8d deletion.\n- A raw root preimage containing old child hashes cannot be regenerated by\n  merely substituting the dimension hash. The essay root was recomputed\n  from its printed AST with the public projection function instead.\n\nNo new architectural defect was found. The pairing/manifest sequencing\nissues above are existing phase-plan boundaries and are kept explicit.\n\n## Files and line counts\n\nTracked-file counts are added/deleted lines from `git diff --numstat`.\n\n| File | Added | Deleted |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| `docs/design/dao.jing.call-site-classification.md` | 19 | 22 |\n| `docs/design/dao.jing.hash-registry.md` | 25 | 39 |\n| `docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.derivations.md` | 1 | 1 |\n| `src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc` | 5 | 5 |\n| `src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc` | 11 | 17 |\n| `src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc` | 11 | 10 |\n| `test/resources/yin/vm/ucf/handoff-v2.txt` | 18 | 18 |\n| `test/yang/python/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc` | 3 | 3 |\n| `test/yang/python/antlr/linked_safepoint_test.cljc` | 3 | 3 |\n| `test/yin/vm/debruijn/stack_parity_test.cljc` | 11 | 10 |\n| `test/yin/vm/debruijn_code_test.cljc` | 5 | 13 |\n| `test/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code_test.cljc` | 1 | 1 |\n| `test/yin/vm/debruijn_register_compile_test.cljc` | 12 | 20 |\n| `test/yin/vm/debruijn_test.cljc` | 8 | 8 |\n| `test/yin/vm/linker_test.cljc` | 15 | 13 |\n| `test/yin/vm/semantic_register/derive_test.cljc` | 11 | 11 |\n| `collab/1792620000000-8ab-regen.clj` (new) | 41 | 0 |\n| `collab/1792620000000-8ab-intermediates.edn` (new) | 1670 | 0 |\n| `collab/1792620000000-engineer-8ab.report.md` (new) | 251 | 0 |\n\n19 files changed: 16 tracked files and 3 new artifacts (this report, the\nreproduction script and the printed-intermediate EDN file). Pre-existing\nuntracked prompt, plan and agent stdout files were left alone.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
