tect-phase8-plan.report.md-165-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-166-**Q1 (OWNER). Who edits the 10 C4 files, and when.** The cutover cannot compile without rewriting `linked_harness.cljc:105-120` and the ten Python tests that require the old kernel, `dl`, `rc` and `handoff`, and without regenerating `manifest-golden`, `pysp-manifest-golden` and verifying the literal-address pins. Options: (a) this track edits them in slice 8f under a frozen C4 branch state the owner declares (the other orchestrator pauses commits to those files for the slice's duration); (b) the other orchestrator ports them against a published 8c/8e API on a C4 branch, and 8f merges both. Recommendation: (a), because the change is mechanical (the harness's three backend lambdas and the loader) and a two-party edit of one file is the worst conflict shape; cost half a day plus the C4 slow lane (hours on a laptop; shiva/jupiter preferred). The owner must also say whether the C4 goldens are \"ours to move\" (derivations §8.1 says publish twice and diff; the review must show the diff).\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-167-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-168-**Q2 (OWNER). Do versions 0/1/2, `handoff.cljc` and `checkpoint.cljc` die in this phase.** The brief says yes (\"leave at phase 8\"). The inventory confirms zero production requirers and 141 tests. Recommendation: yes, in one slice (8d), because keeping a 3783-line codec nobody produces is the legacy the no-compat rule forbids, and because its tests pin the old kernel and so block 8f. Cost: 1.5 days (mostly porting the helpers the new tests borrow from `lift_support`/`v2_support`). The one thing lost is the only existing test of the holder's acceptance of a version-2 body as a refusal; add one row to `rows_test` that a version-2 or version-0 header is `:yin.k/undecodable` (the holder path never dispatched on version; confirm, do not invent).\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-169-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-170-**Q3. Rename mechanics for a name that other tracks and docs cite.** Recommendation: two commits inside slice 8f. Commit 1: `git mv` of 8 source and 16 test files plus `ns` forms, the `:yin.semantic-register/code` keyword to `:yin.semantic/code`, alias `sr` kept where it reads well; no logic change. Commit 2: the 56 requirers' API rewrite. Reviewers diff commit 1 with `--find-renames` and read only commit 2. Docs are a third commit (8g). Keep `yin.vm.semantic-register.*` nowhere, no alias namespace (no compat shim). Cost: 2 days codex, mostly the 58 `vm-load-program` sites.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-171-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-172-**Q4. The descriptor change is two rows, not one.** Derivations §8.1-8.2 say the printed descriptor \"differs from the previous one only by the removed `:dim/lift-to` row\", but the BLAKE3 ruling also flips the `:hash :sha256` row (`debruijn_code.cljc:138`, `debruijn_register_code.cljc:200`, `debruijn.cljc:139-140`). Recommendation: amend §8.1's mechanical check to \"differs by exactly the removed `:dim/lift-to` row and the `:hash` value\", and compute descriptor hashes with `jing/blake3`. No version bump (ruling 2 covers both as regeneration). Cost: zero beyond the doc line; flagged because a reviewer applying §8.1 literally would refuse the slice.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-173-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-174-**Q5. What replaces `yin.vm.code` for `completion.cljc` and `materialize-vector!`.** `completion.cljc:206, :256` project a v3 vector to qualified rows for the completion fold; `publish.cljc` materialises the semantic vector through `code/materialize-vector!`. Recommendation: `materialize-vector!` is one `jing/materialize!` of the vector and moves into `sr-code`; completion gets `sr-code`'s row projection (or `sr-linearize`'s) under the same name. Decide at 8c review whether `completion.cljc` needs a v4 projection at all or whether `completion_test` (3 SHA-256 sites) is testing a dead path. Cost: half a day.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-175-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-176-**Q6 (OWNER). Fate of `docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md`.** It describes the v3 machine that is deleted. Options: (a) delete it and move the §1 stance and the `\"v2\"`/`\"v3\"` revision history into `yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md` §3-5; (b) rewrite its header to \"historical, superseded by `yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md`\", keep body; (c) rename `yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md` to `yin.vm.semantic.md` and delete the old. The frozen design's own header says it \"takes the name `yin.vm.semantic`\". Recommendation: (c) plus a one-paragraph history block, because a doc named after a namespace that no longer exists is the same legacy as a shim. Cost: 1 day of doc work in 8g including the 25 citers.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-177-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-178-**Q7. The old harness and stage tests of the old kernel.** `engine_gate_test`, `semantic_engine_test`, `semantic_ffi_test`, `semantic_stream_observer_test`, `stream_poll_test`, `telemetry_test`, `heap_reclamation_test` etc. exercise the engine through the old kernel. Recommendation: port, do not delete; the new kernel is the same engine's client. Slice 8f carries a coverage audit: list every deftest in deleted files, and for each name a surviving deftest or write one. Reviewer gate: the suite's deftest count after 8f is at least today's minus the 85 + 141 + (91 - ported) that are tests of deleted code, documented in the slice report with the list. Cost: in 8f's 2 days.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-179-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-180-**Q8. Who regenerates the C4 goldens and the literal-address pins.** Covered by Q1; the mechanical check is derivations §8.1 row 6 (publish twice, diff the manifest map). If the five `int_literal_test` and `float_address_test` pins are v3 vector addresses they die; if tree or v4 addresses they hold. Decided at 8f by printing them.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-181-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-182-**Q9. Deletion order (irreversible).** Fixed by this plan: 8a pins and regenerates goldens and moves the H descriptor golden; 8b moves BLAKE3; 8c switches production callers; 8d deletes the old transport; 8e deletes the three old lowerers; 8f deletes the old kernel and renames; 8g documents. Nothing is deleted before its replacement is green on three hosts in the same slice or earlier.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-183-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-184-**Q10. `derive_test`'s `:old` oracle legs** (`:150-160`, `:438-447`, `:612-630` `c4-backends :stack-old/:register-old`). These compare new lowerings against the old lowerers and die with them (8e). The execution oracle then compares `:stack-new`/`:register-new` against the walker and the semantic kernel only (§6.1 already names the walker as oracle). Recommendation: accept; the old lowerers' answers are already pinned as the §6.3 goldens.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-185-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-186----\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-187-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-188-## 3. Slicing\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-189-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-190-Estimates: codex implementation days; review rounds 2-4 per slice (Fable/opus, non-author). Hosts: every slice runs the quick tier on JVM per iteration (`bb test:sub:clj yin.vm` or `clojure -M:test -n <ns>`), `bb test:changed` on three hosts at landing (G2). Slow tier (`bb test:all`), C4 suite with `--slow`, and three hosts once at the phase boundary (8f/8g).\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-191-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-192-| Slice | Files | Depends on | Acceptance (named tests) | Hosts | Codex | Reviews |\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-193-|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-194-| **8a Descriptors and goldens** | `debruijn_code.cljc:145`, `debruijn_register_code.cljc:204` (drop `:dim/lift-to`), `debruijn_code_test.cljc:364-368` (drop two lift assertions, pin descriptor hash), `derive_test.cljc:240, :419-428` (regenerate), `linker_test.cljc:253-260, :522-531` (helpers to `derive`, regenerate), `debruijn_register_code_test.cljc:7`, `debruijn_register_compile_test.cljc:446` (dup golden deleted), `stack_parity_test.cljc:321-347` (producer to `derive`, regenerate) | none | `debruijn-code-test/descriptor-declares-the-contract` (now pins hash), `derive-test/{stack-goldens,register-goldens,stack-determinism,register-determinism,lexical-address-law,lexical-address-law-stack}`, `linke