c/yin/vm` returns none | n/a | 1.5 d | 2 |\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-201-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-202-Ordering and concurrency:\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-203-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-204-| | needs | concurrent with |\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-205-|---|---|---|\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-206-| 8ab | nothing | 8d |\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-207-| 8c | 8ab | 8d |\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-208-| 8d | nothing | 8ab, 8c |\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-209-| 8e | 8c | nothing (touches 37 test files; serialize) |\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-210-| 8f | 8c, 8d, 8e | nothing |\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-211-| 8g | 8f | nothing (docs only; may start drafting during 8f review) |\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-212-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-213-Gate list: quick tier (`bb test:sub:clj yin.vm` per iteration, `bb test:changed` three hosts at landing) for every slice; `bb test:sub yin.vm yin.vm.ucf` at 8c and 8e checkpoints; the slow tier once at 8f on shiva/jupiter plus the C4 suite with `--slow`; three hosts at every landing from 8ab up because the regenerated constants must agree on JVM, Node and Dart (that is what `pinned-identities-are-host-independent` and `register-determinism` exist for).\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-214-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-215-Branching: `srvm-phase8` off `srvm-phase7` (after phase 7 lands on master, rebase once); each slice a branch `srvm-phase8a` etc. merged into `srvm-phase8`; `srvm-phase8` lands on master only after 8g.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-216-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-217----\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-218-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-219-## 4. Risks and mitigations\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-220-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-221-1. **Mass rename collides with the other orchestrator.** 56 files, 10 of them C4's, and `linked_harness.cljc` is the shared hinge. Mitigation: Q1 ruling; freeze window announced via collab/owner relay before 8e starts; 8e and 8f edit C4 files only as mechanical API substitution with no behavioural change; the C4 suite over new images is the proof. Never touch `datomworld-c4-*` worktrees (none exist in `git worktree list` today; the C4 work seems to live in the main checkout's branches).\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-222-2. **Accidental coverage loss when deleting 317 deftests.** Mitigation: Q7 audit list in the 8f report (deleted test name, reason: tests deleted code / ported to X / replaced by Y); port the engine-level tests; reviewer refuses 8f without the list. Count today: 4574.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-223-3. **Hash regeneration drift.** Three regeneration moments collapse into one (8ab merged) so each H/R constant moves once; §8.1's mechanical check is applied by the reviewer on printed intermediates (image, descriptor, manifest map); A addresses in `corpus.cljc` (32) and `rows_test` (20) and the 7a/7b fixtures are asserted unchanged as a negative gate. Descriptor diff is exactly two rows (Q4).\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-224-4. **Dart name resolution on rename.** The new `yin.vm.semantic` compiles to `lib/cljd-out/yin/vm/semantic.dart`, the same path the old kernel occupied; a stale build cache or a stale `semantic_register.dart` referenced by a stale `semantic_register/*.dart` can shadow or double-define. Mitigation: 8f's Dart lane starts with a clean `lib/cljd-out` (and the same on shiva/jupiter before their lanes); the known cljd traps (reader-conditional order, `[_ _]` protocol params, chunked `for`, unary minus) are re-checked by the three-host gate, not by inspection. Also the file rename changes the cljd build's import graph; the Dart peer binary must be rebuilt (`bb build:yin-repl-peer`) before `dht_process_test`.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-225-5. **The REPL custody gap closes by rename, but the REPL also loses `packet->named-datoms`.** `repl.cljc:150-156` feeds the old lowerers from named datoms; after 8c the stack/register evaluators derive from A. A REPL session that `def`s across inputs relies on `append-stack-image`/`append-register-image` (`:159-204`) keeping earlier images; `derive` produces images with the same `:segment`/`:bodies` shape, but `absolute-pc` lookups use `dcode/image-hash`, which moves under BLAKE3 in the same window. Mitigation: `repl_test` and `dht_process_test` in 8c's acceptance; run the REPL smoke on Node (`target/yin-repl.js`) in 8c.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-226-6. **`completion.cljc` and the v3 table (Q5)** may hide a dependency on v3 row shapes in the completion fold; discovered at 8c. Mitigation: `completion_test` in 8c acceptance; if the fold needs a v4 projection that does not exist, 8c's report says so and 8e waits.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-227-7. **Review-round inflation.** Phases 5-7 averaged 2-4 rounds; 8c and 8f are the two slices with the most files and the most hosts. Mitigation: split 8f into two commits (Q3) so the reviewer reads the rename as moves; keep `--find-renames` diffs in the report.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-228-8. **Credits.** Codex implements (gpt-6.1-sol, workspace-write); Fable/opus review only. If codex is out, implementation waits (owner rule); do not move implementation to opus without a ruling.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-229-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-230-**Rollback story.** Every slice is a branch; `srvm-phase8` is not merged to master until 8g. Rolling back a slice is deleting its branch and re-running the predecessor's quick tier. Rolling back after master lands is a `git revert` of the one merge commit; nothing is persisted outside git (dev-only repo, no deployed stores, owner rule). The regenerated goldens and C4 manifests are recomputable from the printed intermediates in each slice report, so no golden is ever \"lost\": the old values are in git history and the new ones in the report.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-231-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-232----\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-233-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-234-## 5. Honest total estimate\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-235-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-236-| | Codex days | Review rounds | Calendar |\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-237-|---|---|---|---|\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-238-| 8ab | 1.5 | 2-3 | 2-3 days |\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-239-| 8c | 3 | 3-4 | 5-6 days |\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-240-| 8d (concurrent) | 1.5 | 2-3 | within 8ab+8c |\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-241-| 8e | 2 | 2-3 | 3-4 days |\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-242-| 8f | 3 | 3-4 | 5-6 days + slow tier (JVM 20+ min, Node/Dart ~5 min each, C4 slow sequence hours on a laptop; use shiva/jupiter) |\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-243-| 8g | 1.5 | 2 | 2-3 days |\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-244-| **Total** | **12.5 (range 11-15)** | **14-19 rounds** | **4-5 weeks** with 8d overlapped; 6 weeks if every slice hits 4 rounds or codex credits lapse |\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-245-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-246-Not counted: the owner's own time on Q1-Q6, and any C4-side rebase the other orchestrator needs after 8f.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-247-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-248----\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-249-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-250-## Verdict\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-251-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-252-**NOT READY.** Blocking owner questions:\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-253-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-254-- **Q1** who edits the 10 C4 files and the two C4 manifest goldens, and the freeze window.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-255-- **Q2** confirm versions 0/1/2, `handoff.cljc` and `checkpoint.cljc` die in 8d (the brief implies yes; the inventory found no production requirer, so a yes costs nothing).\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-256-- **Q4** accept the two-row descriptor diff (lift-to removed, `:hash :blake3`) as the amended §8.1 check.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-257-- **Q6** fate of `docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md` (recommend: the frozen design takes the name, old doc deleted, history block kept).\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-258-\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md-259-Q3, Q5, Q7-Q10 are recommendations the orchestrator can adopt without an owner ruling. On Q1, Q2, Q4, Q6 answered, slice 8ab can be briefed to codex the same day; 8d can be briefed in parallel on Q2 alone.\n(ns yang.python.antlr.linked-prelude-test\n  \"C4 slice P2 (docs/design/yang.antlr.md 8.5.6): the Python runtime\n   profile as the linker module `py`. The module emitter derives one\n   module tree, its exports and its publication spec from the single\n   definition list; the spec declares every free name of the tree, the\n   host exports by profile address; the AST walker's link stays refused\n   until L-b. The published module and the linked runs are\n   `yang.python.antlr.linked-harness`'s: one publication per process,\n   served `:trusted`, so every test that publishes or links is slow.\n\n   Cross-unit exception identity is tested in prelude notation over two\n   units of one task: until I1 Python source has no channel that carries\n   a value from one unit to another, so the Python-source form is I1's.\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n    [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\n    [dao.test-slow :as slow]\n    [yang.python.antlr.linked-harness :as h]\n    [yang.python.antlr.lower :as lower]\n    [yang.python.antlr.lower-portable-test :as portable]\n    [yang.python.antlr.prelude :as prelude]\n    [yang.python.antlr.uast :as u]\n    [yin.vm :as vm]\n    [yin.vm.data :as data]\n    [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n    [yin.vm.integer :as integer]\n    [yin.vm.linker :as linker]\n    [yin.vm.linker.interpreter :as link]\n    [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]\n    [yin.vm.module :as module]))\n\n\n(def ^:private limits\n  {::integer/max-bits 100000, ::integer/max-digits 4300})\n\n\n(def ^:private registry\n  \"The full host registry a Python composition registers.\"\n  (-> (module/empty-registry)\n      module/register-cell-module\n      (data/register-data-module {::data/max-items 1048576})\n      (prelude/register-integer-module limits)))\n\n\n(defn- refusal-of\n  \"The ex-data of what `thunk` throws, or nil when it returns.\"\n  [thunk]\n  (try (thunk)\n       nil\n       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default) e\n         (or (ex-data e) {}))))\n\n\n(defn- def-key\n  \"The literal key of a `(yin/def k v)` application node, else nil.\"\n  [node]\n  (when (and (map? node)\n             (= :application (:type node))\n             (= 'yin/def (get-in node [:operator :name])))\n    (get-in node [:operands 0 :value])))\n\n\n(defn- module-level-keys\n  \"The keys the module tree defines as operands of its one application.\"\n  [ast]\n  (set (keep def-key (:operands ast))))\n\n\n(defn- sexp-def-keys\n  \"Every key a prelude-notation form defines with `(yin/def (quote k) v)`.\"\n  [form]\n  (set (keep (fn [x]\n               (when (and (seq? x) (= 'yin/def (first x)))\n                 (let [k (second x)]\n                   (if (seq? k) (second k) k))))\n             (tree-seq coll? seq form))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The module emitter\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(deftest strip-renames-only-the-module-namespace-test\n  (is (= 'add (prelude/strip 'py/add)))\n  (is (= 'init! (prelude/strip 'py/init!)))\n  (is (= 'py.b/list (prelude/strip 'py.b/list)))\n  (is (= 'py.rt/state (prelude/strip 'py.rt/state)))\n  (is (= 'cell/new (prelude/strip 'cell/new)))\n  (is (= 'x (prelude/strip 'x)))\n  (is (= :py/None (prelude/strip :py/None))))\n\n\n(deftest module-uast-is-one-wide-application-test\n  (let [ast prelude/module-uast\n        operands (:operands ast)\n        op (:operator ast)]\n    (testing \"one application of a lambda returning nil to every definition\"\n      (is (= :application (:type ast)))\n      (is (= :lambda (:type op)))\n      (is (= (count operands) (count (:params op))))\n      (is (= :literal (get-in op [:body :type])))\n      (is (nil? (get-in op [:body :value])))\n      (is (every? some? (map def-key operands))))\n    (testing \"the placeholders come first, sorted, each the literal :py/uninit\"\n      (let [n (count prelude/runtime-keys)\n            placeholders (take n operands)]\n        (is (= prelude/runtime-keys (mapv def-key placeholders)))\n        (is (every? #(= {:type :literal, :value :py/uninit}\n                        (dissoc (get-in % [:operands 1]) :tail?))\n                    placeholders))))\n    (testing \"then every definition, stripped, in definition order\"\n      (is (= (mapv (comp prelude/strip first) prelude/definitions)\n             (mapv def-key (drop (count prelude/runtime-keys) operands)))))\n    (testing \"no symbol of the module's own namespace survives stripping\"\n      (is (not-any? (fn [x]\n                      (and (symbol? x) (= \"py\" (namespace x))))\n                    (tree-seq coll? seq ast))))\n    (testing \"Rule R holds over the module tree\"\n      (is (nil? (vm/ast-reserved-defect ast))))))\n\n\n(deftest module-exports-test\n  (testing \"every py/ key of the definition list, stripped; no internal key\"\n    (is (= (set (keep (fn [[k _]]\n                        (when (= \"py\" (namespace k)) (prelude/strip k)))\n                      prelude/definitions))\n           prelude/module-exports))\n    (is (every? #(contains? prelude/module-exports %)\n                '[init! run-main run-module object-class vconj lnot]))\n    (is (not-any? namespace prelude/module-exports))\n    (is (not (contains? prelude/module-exports 'state))))\n  (testing \"D4: no export is a primitive name\"\n    (is (empty? (filter #(contains? vm/primitives %)\n                        prelude/module-exports)))))\n\n\n(deftest module-spec-test\n  (let [spec (prelude/module-spec registry)]\n    (is (= 'py (:name spec) prelude/module-name))\n    (is (= prelude/module-uast (:ast spec)))\n    (is (= prelude/module-exports (:exports spec)))\n    (is (= {} (:requires spec)))\n    (testing \"a host export is declared by its registry profile and effects\"\n      (is (= {:yin.k/profile (get-in module/cell-profiles\n                                     ['new :yin.k/profile]),\n              :yin.k/effects #{:cell/new}}\n             (get-in spec [:primitives 'cell/new])))\n      (is (= #{} (get-in spec [:primitives 'integer/add :yin.k/effects]))))\n    (testing \"a primitive is declared by its vm/primitives profile\"\n      (is (= (vm/profile-of vm/primitives '+)\n             (get-in spec [:primitives '+])))))\n  (testing \"a free name no registry module or primitive supplies is refused\n            before anything is published\"\n    (let [no-data (-> (module/empty-registry)\n                      module/register-cell-module\n                      (prelude/register-integer-module limits))\n          refusal (refusal-of #(prelude/module-spec no-data))]\n      (is (= :yang.python.antlr/undeclared-free\n             (:yang.python.antlr/refusal refusal)))\n      (is (= \"data\" (namespace (:name refusal)))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; A8. The host-export declaration is derived and complete\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(deftest module-spec-declares-every-free-name-test\n  (let [declared (keys (:primitives (prelude/module-spec registry)))]\n    (testing \"the qualified declarations are exactly the host names (I7)\"\n      (is (= prelude/host-names (set (filter namespace declared)))))\n    (testing \"the bare declarations are primitives\"\n      (is (every? #(contains? vm/primitives %) (remove namespace declared))))\n    (testing \"the exports are no primitive and all defined at module level\"\n      (is (empty? (filter #(contains? vm/primitives %)\n                          prelude/module-exports)))\n      (is (every? (module-level-keys prelude/module-uast)\n                  prelude/module-exports)))\n    (testing \"the runtime keys are what the generated py/init! defines,\n              the ready flag aside\"\n      (is (= (set prelude/runtime-keys)\n             (disj (sexp-def-keys (get (into {} prelude/definitions)\n                                       'py/init!))\n                   'py.rt/state)))\n      (is (= 65 (count prelude/runtime-keys))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; A12. The module tree fits the default bounds with headroom\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- deepest-occurrence\n  \"The longest occurrence path from the root of the canonical rows `bc`:\n   every row id a row names is a child occurrence.\"\n  [{:keys [root rows]}]\n  (loop [frontier [[root 0]]\n         deepest 0]\n    (if (empty? frontier)\n      deepest\n      (let [[id depth] (peek frontier)\n            kids (filter #(contains? rows %)\n                         (tree-seq coll? seq (vec (rest (get rows id)))))]\n        (recur (into (pop frontier) (map (fn [k] [k (inc depth)])) kids)\n               (max deepest depth))))))\n\n\n(deftest module-tree-fits-the-default-bounds-with-headroom-test\n  (let [bc (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode prelude/module-uast)\n        rows (count (:rows bc))\n        depth (deepest-occurrence bc)]\n    (testing \"the row count is below half the parts bound\"\n      (is (< rows (quot (:max-parts linker/default-bounds) 2))\n          (str rows \" rows\")))\n    (testing \"the deepest occurrence is below half the depth bound\"\n      (is (< depth (quot (:max-depth linker/default-bounds) 2))\n          (str depth \" deep\")))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; A1 and A10. `py` publishes to one pinned manifest address; the walker is\n;; excluded, visibly\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private manifest-golden\n  \"I1 moved this once: the definition list gained the module runtime\n   (`py/import`, module objects, sys.modules and its two pre-seeded\n   modules) and the `ImportError` class. I2 moved it once: py/import-sub,\n   py/import-from, py/import-star, py/import-fail and their helpers, and\n   a top-level module's `__package__` ''. I3 moved it once:\n   py/star-item, `__all__` read by index (ranges included), and\n   py/run-session, the REPL `__main__` runner. It moved once more with\n   the rebase onto master 4529b5bd: the profile digest in the manifest\n   uses BLAKE3 since 492ff50b. Phase 8ab regenerates the H/R\n   checksums, derivation records and index keys.\"\n  (keyword (str \"segment/blake3-\"\n                \"577aabfb863288b6f7aefbbb4c299befdf4825953aa7ccaa49a55428e26517ee\")))\n\n\n(def ^:private vector-formats\n  [:yin.semantic/code :yin.debruijn.code :yin.debruijn.register])\n\n\n(defn- manifest-address\n  []\n  (let [{:keys [store result address]} @h/published\n        links (:links result)]\n    (testing \"one address on every host (JVM golden)\"\n      (is (= manifest-golden address) (pr-str (dissoc result :links :walk))))\n    (testing \"the three vector formats link :ok under :verifying\"\n      (doseq [f vector-formats]\n        (is (= :ok (get-in links [f :status])) (str f))\n        (is (= :verified (get-in links [f :trust])) (str f))))\n    (testing \"publishing twice into one store answers one address\"\n      (is (= address\n             (:address (publish/publish-module!\n                         store (prelude/module-spec registry))))))))\n\n\n(deftest ^:slow manifest-address-test\n  (slow/guard \"manifest-address-test\" manifest-address))\n\n\n(defn- walker-is-excluded\n  []\n  (let [walker (get-in @h/published [:result :links :yin.ast/code])]\n    (testing \"the AST walker is refused :undeclared-free on a sibling read\n              until L-b; L-b's landing flips this assertion\"\n      (is (= :refused (:status walker)))\n      (is (= :undeclared-free (:reason walker)))\n      (is (= 'float? (:name walker)) \"the first retained py key\")\n      (is (contains? prelude/module-exports (:name walker))))))\n\n\n(deftest ^:slow walker-is-excluded-test\n  (slow/guard \"walker-is-excluded-test\" walker-is-excluded))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; A3. One source under two prelude revisions keeps one program root\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- statement\n  [expr-stmt]\n  [:stmt [:simple_stmts [:simple_stmt expr-stmt] [\"NEWLINE\" \"\\n\"]]])\n\n\n(defn- chain\n  [rules leaf]\n  (reduce (fn [inner r] [r inner]) leaf (reverse rules)))\n\n\n(def ^:private expr-chain\n  [:testlist_star_expr :test :or_test :and_test :not_test :comparison :expr\n   :atom_expr :atom])\n\n\n(def ^:private x-equals-1\n  \"`x = 1`, as the parser's CST packet.\"\n  (portable/packet [:file_input\n                    (statement [:expr_stmt\n                                (chain expr-chain [:name [\"NAME\" \"x\"]])\n                                [\"ASSIGN\" \"=\"]\n                                (chain expr-chain [\"NUMBER\" \"1\"])])\n                    [\"EOF\" \"<EOF>\"]]))\n\n\n(def ^:private linked-x-equals-1\n  (lower/lower-packet x-equals-1 {:prelude :linked}))\n\n\n(def ^:private program-root-golden\n  (keyword (str \"segment/blake3-\"\n                \"dbe72b291a26a4f594ad55cf52e5ffd0\"\n                \"88fdd262b58fd26212a01a7dd983a6df\")))\n\n\n(defn- holds-no-prelude\n  \"The linked program `ast` holds no definition, no runtime key and no\n   prelude row.\"\n  [ast]\n  (let [nodes (tree-seq coll? seq ast)\n        symbols (filter symbol? nodes)\n        prelude-rows (set (:operands prelude/module-uast))]\n    (is (not-any? #{'yin/def} symbols))\n    (is (not-any? #(contains? #{\"py.b\" \"py.rt\"} (namespace %))\n                  (filter namespace symbols)))\n    (is (not-any? #(contains? prelude-rows %) nodes))))\n\n\n(defn- with-probe\n  \"`spec` with one more definition, `probe`, appended and exported.\"\n  [spec]\n  (-> spec\n      (update-in [:ast :operator :params] conj '%probe)\n      (update-in [:ast :operands] conj (u/def! 'probe (u/lit :py/uninit)))\n      (update :exports conj 'probe)))\n\n\n(defn- program-root-is-prelude-independent\n  []\n  (let [root (:root (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode linked-x-equals-1))\n        revised (publish/publish-module! (mem/create-content-mem)\n                                         (with-probe\n                                           (prelude/module-spec registry)))]\n    (testing \"the linked program root is one address on every host (JVM\n              golden)\"\n      (is (= program-root-golden root) (str root)))\n    (testing \"a prelude revision moves the manifest address only\"\n      (is (some? (:address revised)) (pr-str (dissoc revised :links :walk)))\n      (is (not= (:address @h/published) (:address revised)))\n      (is (= root (:root (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode\n                           (lower/lower-packet x-equals-1\n                                               {:prelude :linked}))))))\n    (testing \"the program tree holds no prelude\"\n      (holds-no-prelude linked-x-equals-1))))\n\n\n(deftest ^:slow program-root-is-prelude-independent-test\n  (slow/guard \"program-root-is-prelude-independent-test\"\n              program-root-is-prelude-independent))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; A4. Cross-unit exception identity\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private unit-1\n  (u/mark-tails\n    (u/sexp->uast\n      '(do (require (quote py))\n           (py/init!)\n           (yin/def (quote u1-exc)\n             (py/try (fn []\n                       (py/raise\n                         (py/call (py/global-get (py/dict-new)\n                                                 {:py/str \"ValueError\"})\n                                  [])))\n                     (fn [e] e)\n                     (fn [] :py/None)))\n           (yin/def (quote u1-cls)\n             (py/global-get (py/dict-new) {:py/str \"Exception\"}))))))\n\n\n(def ^:private unit-2\n  (u/mark-tails\n    (u/sexp->uast\n      '(do (require (quote py))\n           (py/init!)\n           (conj (conj []\n                       (py/isinstance u1-exc\n                                      (py/global-get (py/dict-new)\n                                                     {:py/str \"Exception\"})))\n                 (= u1-cls (py/global-get (py/dict-new)\n                                          {:py/str \"Exception\"})))))))\n\n\n(defn- exception-class-is-shared-across-units\n  []\n  (doseq [k (keys h/backends)]\n    (testing (name k)\n      (let [pair (link/make-pair)\n            src (h/source)\n            [t1 pair] (h/drive ((get h/backends k)\n                                unit-1\n                                (h/composition (h/registry) pair))\n                               pair src)\n            [t2 _] (h/drive ((get h/continues k) t1 unit-2) pair src)]\n        (is (vm/halted? t1))\n        (testing \"the second require answers from the registry and the\n                  second init! allocates nothing\"\n          (is (= [true true] (vm/value t2))))))))\n\n\n(deftest ^:slow exception-class-is-shared-across-units-test\n  (slow/guard \"exception-class-is-shared-across-units-test\"\n              exception-class-is-shared-across-units))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; A5. An install child at `validated` has an empty heap and no lift refusal\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- install-child-defines-only\n  []\n  (let [{:keys [result address]} @h/published\n        exports (sort-by str prelude/module-exports)]\n    (doseq [[k f] (map vector [:semantic :stack :register] vector-formats)]\n      (testing (name k)\n        (let [parent ((get h/backends k)\n                      (u/lit nil)\n                      (h/composition (h/registry) (link/make-pair)))\n              child (vm/run (module/spawn-module\n                              parent\n                              (get-in result [:links f :value])\n                              {:modules (:modules parent),\n                               :origin :t0.0,\n                               :ancestry ['py],\n                               :capability-secret \"child\"}))\n              store (vm/store child)]\n          (is (vm/halted? child))\n          (is (not (vm/blocked? child)))\n          (is (empty? (:heap child)))\n          (is (every? #(contains? store %) exports))\n          (is (= :py/uninit (get store 'py.rt/state)))\n          (let [lifted (engine/lift-slice child address exports)]\n            (is (= [address] (keys (:stores lifted))))\n            (is (empty? (:cells lifted)))))))))\n\n\n(deftest ^:slow install-child-defines-only-test\n  (slow/guard \"install-child-defines-only-test\" install-child-defines-only))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; A6. A wrong host-module profile is refused by name\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- wrong-host-profile-refuses-the-require\n  []\n  (let [pure-new (vm/primitive-profile 'new :pure [1] #{} :none)\n        modules (-> (module/default-registry)\n                    (module/register-host-module\n                      'cell module/cell-module\n                      (assoc module/cell-profiles 'new pure-new))\n                    (data/register-data-module {::data/max-items 1048576})\n                    (prelude/register-integer-module limits))]\n    (doseq [k (keys h/backends)]\n      (testing (name k)\n        (let [refusal (refusal-of #(h/run-linked k linked-x-equals-1\n                                                 {:modules modules}))]\n          (is (= :unresolved-free (:reason refusal)) (pr-str refusal))\n          (is (= 'cell/new (:name refusal))))))))\n\n\n(deftest ^:slow wrong-host-profile-refuses-the-require-test\n  (slow/guard \"wrong-host-profile-refuses-the-require-test\"\n              wrong-host-profile-refuses-the-require))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; A7. A missing name-environment entry is refused with no bundled fallback\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- absent-name-refuses-with-no-fallback\n  []\n  (holds-no-prelude linked-x-equals-1)\n  (doseq [k (keys h/backends)]\n    (testing (name k)\n      (let [pair (link/make-pair)\n            task (vm/run ((get h/backends k)\n                          linked-x-equals-1\n                          (h/composition (h/registry) pair)))\n            served (link/serve {:pair pair, :source (h/source {})})\n            refusal (refusal-of #(vm/run task))\n            held (keys (vm/store task))]\n        (is (empty? (:pending served)))\n        (is (= :absent (:reason refusal)) (pr-str refusal))\n        (is (= 'py (:name refusal)))\n        (testing \"the task's store holds no prelude key\"\n          (is (not-any? #(contains? prelude/module-exports %) held))\n          (is (not-any? #(and (symbol? %)\n                              (contains? #{\"py\" \"py.b\" \"py.rt\"} (namespace %)))\n                        held)))))))\n\n\n(deftest ^:slow absent-name-refuses-with-no-fallback-test\n  (slow/guard \"absent-name-refuses-with-no-fallback-test\"\n              absent-name-refuses-with-no-fallback))\n(ns yang.python.antlr.linked-safepoint-test\n  \"C4 slice P3 (docs/design/yang.antlr.md 8.5.6): the hook prelude as the\n   linker module `pysp`. The module emitter derives one module tree, its\n   exports and its publication spec from the same definition list the\n   bundled hook prelude loads; the spec declares every free name the tree\n   reads but the `py/*` exports, which its pinned `py` requirement covers.\n\n   Safepoint slice 1's signal acceptance and slice 2's recursion acceptance\n   re-run under the linked profile on the three vector VMs (the walker's\n   link stays refused until L-b), with the lowering's site marks preserved\n   through the stage, the stage's input carrying no prelude row, and a\n   derived program with no `pysp` binding failing closed on the unresolved\n   hook name. Both modules are `yang.python.antlr.linked-harness`'s: one\n   publication per process, served `:trusted`, so every test that publishes\n   or links is slow.\"\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.test-slow :as slow]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [yang.python.antlr.linked-harness :as h]\n            [yang.python.antlr.lower :as lower]\n            [yang.python.antlr.prelude :as prelude]\n            [yang.python.antlr.render :as render]\n            [yang.python.antlr.safepoint :as hooks]\n            [yang.python.antlr.safepoint-programs :as programs]\n            [yang.python.antlr.uast :as u]\n            [yang.safepoint :as safepoint]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.data :as data]\n            [yin.vm.encoder :as encoder]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\n\n\n(defn- refusal-of\n  \"The ex-data of what `thunk` throws, or nil when it returns.\"\n  [thunk]\n  (try (thunk)\n       nil\n       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default) e\n         (or (ex-data e) {}))))\n\n\n(defn- def-key\n  \"The literal key of a `(yin/def k v)` application node, else nil.\"\n  [node]\n  (when (and (map? node)\n             (= :application (:type node))\n             (= 'yin/def (get-in node [:operator :name])))\n    (get-in node [:operands 0 :value])))\n\n\n(defn- nodes\n  \"Every node of map AST `ast`.\"\n  [ast]\n  (tree-seq map?\n            (fn [n] (filter map? (mapcat #(if (vector? %) % [%]) (vals n))))\n            ast))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The linked stage: marks in, no prelude rows, hooks out\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- envelope\n  \"The lowering's linked program batch for `pk`.\"\n  [pk]\n  (let [[_ [[port e]]] (lower/lower-transform {:prelude :linked} pk)]\n    (assert (= :program port))\n    e))\n\n\n(defn- derive*\n  \"`{:projected p :derived e' :record r}` for `pk` under `profile`.\"\n  [pk profile]\n  (let [projected (encoder/project (envelope pk))\n        {:keys [envelope record]} (safepoint/derive-envelope projected profile\n                                                             :test/derived)]\n    {:projected projected, :derived envelope, :record record}))\n\n\n(defn- tree-of\n  [e]\n  (nth (:yin/batch e) (:yin/root e)))\n\n\n(defn- holds-no-prelude\n  \"The linked program `ast` holds no definition, no runtime key and no\n   prelude or hook-prelude row.\"\n  [ast]\n  (let [all (nodes ast)\n        symbols (filter symbol? (tree-seq coll? seq ast))\n        module-rows (into (set (:operands prelude/module-uast))\n                          (:operands hooks/module-uast))]\n    (is (not-any? #{'yin/def} symbols))\n    (is (not-any? #(contains? #{\"py.b\" \"py.rt\" \"py.sp\"} (namespace %))\n                  (filter namespace symbols)))\n    (is (not-any? #(contains? module-rows %) all))))\n\n\n(defn- hook-names-in\n  \"The `pysp` hook names the derived tree applies.\"\n  [ast]\n  (set (keep #(when (and (= :variable (:type %))\n                         (= \"pysp\" (namespace (:name %))))\n                (:name %))\n             (nodes ast))))\n\n\n(deftest stage-input-contains-no-prelude-row-test\n  (doseq [[pk expected] [[programs/while-true-pass #{'pysp/loop}]\n                         [programs/caught #{'pysp/loop}]\n                         [programs/def-and-while\n                          #{'pysp/loop 'pysp/call 'pysp/return}]\n                         [programs/recursion #{'pysp/call 'pysp/return}]]]\n    (let [{:keys [projected derived]} (derive* pk hooks/linked-profile)]\n      (testing \"the stage's input and output carry no prelude row\"\n        (holds-no-prelude (vm/semantic-bytecode->ast (tree-of projected)))\n        (holds-no-prelude (vm/semantic-bytecode->ast (tree-of derived))))\n      (testing \"the derived tree applies exactly the module's hooks\"\n        (is (= expected\n               (hook-names-in (vm/semantic-bytecode->ast\n                                (tree-of derived)))))))))\n\n\n(deftest insertion-is-deterministic-test\n  (doseq [pk [programs/while-true-pass programs/def-and-while]]\n    (is (= (derive* pk hooks/linked-profile)\n           (derive* pk hooks/linked-profile)))))\n\n\n(deftest marks-reach-the-side-table-test\n  (let [{:keys [projected derived]} (derive* programs/def-and-while\n                                             hooks/linked-profile)]\n    (testing \"the linked lowering marks the function's code lambda and the\n              loop lambda exactly as the bundled one does\"\n      (let [marks (filter #(= :yang/site (nth % 3))\n                          (:yin/frontend-metadata projected))]\n        (is (= [:call :loop] (sort (map #(nth % 4) marks))))))\n    (testing \"every derived row validates\"\n      (is (nil? (vm/validate-rows (tree-of derived)))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The module emitter\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(deftest pysp-module-uast-is-one-wide-application-test\n  (let [ast hooks/module-uast\n        operands (:operands ast)\n        op (:operator ast)]\n    (testing \"one application of a lambda returning nil to every definition\"\n      (is (= :application (:type ast)))\n      (is (= :lambda (:type op)))\n      (is (= (count operands) (count (:params op))))\n      (is (= :literal (get-in op [:body :type])))\n      (is (nil? (get-in op [:body :value])))\n      (is (every? some? (map def-key operands))))\n    (testing \"the placeholders come first, sorted, each the literal\n              :py/uninit\"\n      (let [n (count hooks/runtime-keys)\n            placeholders (take n operands)]\n        (is (= (mapv hooks/strip hooks/runtime-keys)\n               (mapv def-key placeholders)))\n        (is (every? #(= {:type :literal, :value :py/uninit}\n                        (dissoc (get-in % [:operands 1]) :tail?))\n                    placeholders))))\n    (testing \"then every definition, stripped, in definition order\"\n      (is (= (mapv (comp hooks/strip first) hooks/function-definitions)\n             (mapv def-key (drop (count hooks/runtime-keys) operands)))))\n    (testing \"no symbol of the module's own namespace survives stripping\"\n      (is (not-any? (fn [x]\n                      (and (symbol? x) (= \"py.sp\" (namespace x))))\n                    (tree-seq coll? seq ast))))\n    (testing \"`py/*` references stay qualified: they are the base prelude's\n              exports, resolved through the registry\"\n      (is (some (fn [x] (and (symbol? x) (= \"py\" (namespace x))))\n                (tree-seq coll? seq ast))))\n    (testing \"Rule R holds over the module tree\"\n      (is (nil? (vm/ast-reserved-defect ast))))))\n\n\n(deftest pysp-module-exports-test\n  (testing \"every py.sp/ key of the definition list, stripped; no internal\n            key\"\n    (is (= (set (map (comp hooks/strip first) hooks/function-definitions))\n           hooks/module-exports))\n    (is (every? #(contains? hooks/module-exports %)\n                '[attach! loop call return set-handler!\n                  set-recursion-limit! recursion-limit class]))\n    (is (not-any? namespace hooks/module-exports))\n    (is (not (contains? hooks/module-exports 'handler)))\n    (is (not (contains? hooks/module-exports 'cursor))))\n  (testing \"no export is a primitive name\"\n    (is (empty? (filter #(contains? vm/primitives %)\n                        hooks/module-exports)))))\n\n\n(def ^:private py-address\n  \"A stand-in manifest address: the spec builder only pins it, and no fast\n   test may force a publication.\"\n  :test/py-address)\n\n\n(deftest pysp-module-spec-test\n  (let [spec (hooks/module-spec (h/registry) py-address)]\n    (is (= 'pysp (:name spec) hooks/module-name))\n    (is (= hooks/module-uast (:ast spec)))\n    (is (= hooks/module-exports (:exports spec)))\n    (testing \"the pinned requirement is py at its manifest address\"\n      (is (= {'py py-address} (:requires spec))))\n    (testing \"a py-qualified free name is never a primitive declaration:\n              the requirement covers it\"\n      (is (empty? (filter #(= \"py\" (namespace %))\n                          (keys (:primitives spec))))))\n    (testing \"the qualified declarations are exactly the host names\"\n      (is (= hooks/host-names\n             (set (filter namespace (keys (:primitives spec)))))))\n    (testing \"a host export is declared by its registry profile and effects\"\n      (is (every? #(and (contains? % :yin.k/profile)\n                        (contains? % :yin.k/effects))\n                  (keep #(get-in spec [:primitives %])\n                        (filter namespace (keys (:primitives spec))))))))\n  (testing \"a free name no registry module or primitive supplies is refused\n            before anything is published\"\n    (let [no-cell (-> (module/empty-registry)\n                      (data/register-data-module {::data/max-items 1048576})\n                      (prelude/register-integer-module h/integer-limits))\n          refusal (refusal-of #(hooks/module-spec no-cell py-address))]\n      (is (= :yang.python.antlr/undeclared-free\n             (:yang.python.antlr/refusal refusal)))\n      (is (= \"cell\" (namespace (:name refusal)))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; A1. `pysp` publishes to one pinned manifest address\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private pysp-manifest-golden\n  \"I1, I2 and I3 each moved this once: the pinned `py` requirement is\n   py's own manifest address, which each slice's prelude change moved,\n   and the BLAKE3 profile digest of 492ff50b moved again. Phase 8ab\n   regenerates H/R and the pinned py requirement.\"\n  (keyword (str \"segment/blake3-\"\n                \"6c39c4b94a086de50cff3bc780a9159870d5f1ef4aed47ad2f09846bc500bcf0\")))\n\n\n(defn- pysp-manifest-address\n  []\n  (let [{:keys [store result address]} @h/published-pysp\n        links (:links result)]\n    (testing \"one address on every host (JVM golden)\"\n      (is (= pysp-manifest-golden address) (pr-str (dissoc result :links))))\n    (testing \"the three vector formats link :ok under :verifying\"\n      (doseq [f [:yin.semantic/code :yin.debruijn.code\n                 :yin.debruijn.register]]\n        (is (= :ok (get-in links [f :status])) (str f))))\n    (testing \"publishing twice into one store answers one address\"\n      (is (= address\n             (:address (publish/publish-module!\n                         store (hooks/module-spec (h/registry)\n                                                  (:address @h/published)))))))))\n\n\n(deftest ^:slow pysp-manifest-address-test\n  (slow/guard \"pysp-manifest-address-test\" pysp-manifest-address))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Running A' linked\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- outcome\n  \"A finished run as `[halted? blocked? rendered-value]`.\"\n  [task]\n  [(vm/halted? task) (vm/blocked? task) (render/output (vm/value task))])\n\n\n(defn- with-signals\n  \"A linked `prep` handing the task a signal stream holding `signals`.\"\n  [signals]\n  (fn [task]\n    (let [handle (tu/new-stream 8)]\n      (doseq [s signals] (stream/append! handle s))\n      (let [[ref task] (engine/attach-resource task handle)]\n        (assoc-in task [:store hooks/signals-key] ref)))))\n\n\n(defn- derived-ast\n  \"`A'` for `pk` under the linked profile.\"\n  [pk]\n  (vm/semantic-bytecode->ast\n    (tree-of (:derived (derive* pk hooks/linked-profile)))))\n\n\n(defn- on-every-vm\n  \"Every vector VM's outcome for `ast` under `signals`, or the throw; the\n   composition serves both modules.\"\n  ([ast] (on-every-vm ast []))\n  ([ast signals]\n   (into {}\n         (map (fn [k]\n                [k (try (outcome (h/run-linked\n                                   k ast\n                                   {:link-source (h/safepoint-source),\n                                    :prep (with-signals signals)}))\n                        (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default) e\n                          [:thrown (ex-message e)]))]))\n         (keys h/backends))))\n\n\n(defn- every=\n  [expected results]\n  (doseq [[k result] results]\n    (is (= expected result) (str k))))\n\n\n(defn- linked-run\n  \"The wrapped derived program of `pk` on every VM under `signals`.\"\n  [pk signals]\n  (on-every-vm (hooks/linked-program (derived-ast pk)) signals))\n\n\n(defn- limited-run\n  \"The wrapped derived program of `pk` under recursion limit `n`.\"\n  [pk n signals]\n  (on-every-vm\n    (hooks/linked-program\n      (u/then (u/sexp->uast (list 'pysp/set-recursion-limit! n))\n              (derived-ast pk)))\n    signals))\n\n\n(defn- fail-closed\n  []\n  (testing \"the derived linked program with no `pysp` binding names the\n            hook\"\n    (every= [:thrown \"Unable to resolve symbol: pysp/loop in this context\"]\n            (on-every-vm (derived-ast programs/while-true-pass)))))\n\n\n(deftest ^:slow linked-fail-closed-test\n  (slow/guard \"linked-fail-closed-test\" fail-closed))\n\n\n(defn- interrupt\n  []\n  (testing \"while True: pass with one pre-appended signal ends with\n            KeyboardInterrupt\"\n    (every= [true false {:py/out [], :py/exception {:type \"KeyboardInterrupt\",\n                                                    :args []}}]\n            (linked-run programs/while-true-pass [2])))\n  (testing \"wrapped in try/except KeyboardInterrupt, the handler prints\"\n    (every= [true false {:py/out [\"caught\"], :py/exception nil}]\n            (linked-run programs/caught [2]))))\n\n\n(deftest ^:slow linked-interrupt-test\n  (slow/guard \"linked-interrupt-test\" interrupt))\n\n\n(defn- no-park\n  []\n  (testing \"with an empty signal stream the derived program finishes without\n            blocking and prints what the naive one prints\"\n    (every= [true false {:py/out [\"5\"], :py/exception nil}]\n            (linked-run programs/def-and-while []))))\n\n\n(deftest ^:slow linked-no-park-test\n  (slow/guard \"linked-no-park-test\" no-park))\n\n\n(defn- registered-handler-runs\n  []\n  (testing \"a registered Python handler is called with the signal and None,\n            and the program goes on; registered after `pysp/attach!`, so\n            `py/make-function` builds the function object\"\n    (let [set-handler (u/sexp->uast\n                        '(pysp/set-handler!\n                           (py/make-function \"h\" {:params [\"s\" \"f\"]} [] []\n                                             (fn [args] (py/print (py/vconj [] (py/arg args 0)))))))\n          ast (hooks/linked-program\n                (u/then set-handler (derived-ast programs/def-and-while)))]\n      (every= [true false {:py/out [\"7\" \"5\"], :py/exception nil}]\n              (on-every-vm ast [7])))))\n\n\n(deftest ^:slow linked-registered-handler-test\n  (slow/guard \"linked-registered-handler-test\" registered-handler-runs))\n\n\n(defn- recursion-error\n  []\n  (testing \"the default limit through the module boundary: f(999) is 1000\n            frames and completes; f(1000) raises RecursionError, caught by\n            except; probe(1) finds the limit at 1000 frames\"\n    (every= [true false {:py/out [\"0\" \"rec\" \"1000\"], :py/exception nil}]\n            (linked-run programs/recursion []))))\n\n\n(deftest ^:slow linked-recursion-error-test\n  (slow/guard \"linked-recursion-error-test\" recursion-error))\n\n\n(defn- escape-restores-depth\n  []\n  (testing \"under limit 100: a raise through 50 frames with finally\n            restores the depth saved at the catching try (probe finds 100\n            frames again), and a finally thunk runs at its frame's depth\"\n    (every= [true false {:py/out [\"unwound\" \"100\" \"89\" \"100\" \"99\" \"100\"],\n                         :py/exception nil}]\n            (limited-run programs/unwind 100 []))))\n\n\n(deftest ^:slow linked-escape-restores-depth-test\n  (slow/guard \"linked-escape-restores-depth-test\" escape-restores-depth))\n\n\n(defn- generator-depth\n  []\n  (testing \"under limit 100: depth measures the current continuation across\n            the module boundary as it does bundled — a generator resumed 20\n            frames down runs on top of its resumer, is rebased by a later\n            resume, and every crossing back restores the caller's record\"\n    (every= [true false {:py/out [\"79\" \"99\" \"100\" \"79\" \"100\" \"79\" \"99\"\n                                  \"100\"],\n                         :py/exception nil}]\n            (limited-run programs/generators 100 []))))\n\n\n(deftest ^:slow linked-generator-depth-test\n  (slow/guard \"linked-generator-depth-test\" generator-depth))\n(ns yang.python.antlr.dht-import-test\n  \"C4 slice I3 (docs/design/yang.antlr.md 8.5.6): Python modules published\n   by name and imported over the DHT.\n\n   The fast tests pin the publication: a unit set publishes bottom-up, a\n   cyclic pair is refused by name before anything is written, an import\n   no unit or publication supplies is refused.\n\n   The slow test is the acceptance over the `dao.jing.dht` mesh seam, the\n   in-process form `yin.vm.linker.dht-end-to-end-test` uses, so it runs on\n   the JVM, Node and Dart alike. What travels is the JVM's publication:\n   the artifact `yang.python.antlr.dht-import-fixture` reads, written on\n   the JVM by its generator script -- the guest blobs, manifest addresses\n   and signed envelopes of `A`'s units and `B`'s name, and the importer\n   packets. No host republishes it: the publisher node serves the\n   artifact's bytes and envelopes as they are. Each host also publishes\n   the same packets itself, into a store of its own, and must arrive at\n   the artifact: a host-specific publication difference fails there.\n   `py` is the runtime every node has installed, one manifest address on\n   every host (`linked-prelude-test`'s golden, and the artifact's), since\n   its code images exceed the DHT's message bound.\n\n   One reader, handed `A`'s index manifest and declaring `A`, imports\n   through the DHT link source on the semantic, stack and register VMs.\n   Then `B` vouches for a module, and the reader, declaring `B` too, is\n   refused it by the default admission interpreter while it trusts only `A`\n   (yin.vm.linker.dht.md 7.5), raising ImportError in Python with no install\n   child and no output, and allowed it once it trusts `B`. Next, `B`'s head\n   moves the name to another module between the admission question and its\n   answer: the allow binds the module the question was asked about. Last,\n   `A`'s republication of `k` is indexed, and the reader's import of `t`,\n   which pinned the old `k`, encounters a dependency pin mismatch at\n   statement-time receive when `k` is delivered, raising ImportError before `k`\n   is installed or runs.\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n    [dao.datom :as datom]\n    [dao.jing :as jing]\n    [dao.jing.dht :as jing.dht]\n    [dao.jing.dht.mesh :as mesh]\n    [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\n    [dao.space.dht :as dht]\n    [dao.space.dht-test :as dht-test]\n    [dao.space.index :as index]\n    [dao.stream :as stream]\n    [dao.test-slow :as slow]\n    [yang.python.antlr.dht-import-fixture :as fixture]\n    [yang.python.antlr.import-programs :as programs]\n    [yang.python.antlr.linked-harness :as h]\n    [yang.python.antlr.lower :as lower]\n    [yang.python.antlr.publication :as publication]\n    [yang.python.antlr.render :as render]\n    [yin.vm :as vm]\n    [yin.vm.linker.admission :as admission]\n    [yin.vm.linker.dht :as ld]\n    [yin.vm.linker.head :as head]\n    [yin.vm.linker.interpreter :as link]\n    [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]\n    [yin.vm.linker.sign :as sign]\n    [yin.vm.module :as module]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The fast tests: publication order, cycles, admission\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private stand-in-address\n  \"A stand-in `py` address: a refused publication never reads it.\"\n  :test/address)\n\n\n(defn- unit\n  [nm pk]\n  {:name nm, :packet pk, :package? false})\n\n\n(deftest units-publish-after-what-they-import-test\n  (testing \"t imports k: k is ordered first whatever the input order\"\n    (is (= {:status :ok, :order [\"k\" \"t\" \"m\"]}\n           (publication/publication-order\n             [(unit \"t\" programs/t-packet) (unit \"k\" programs/k-packet)\n              (unit \"m\" programs/m-packet)]\n             {}))))\n  (testing \"an import a publication already supplies needs no unit\"\n    (is (= {:status :ok, :order [\"t\"]}\n           (publication/publication-order [(unit \"t\" programs/t-packet)]\n                                          {\"k\" :test/k})))))\n\n\n(deftest a-cyclic-pair-is-refused-at-publication-by-name-test\n  (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n        refusal {:status :refused,\n                 :reason :yang.python.antlr/import-cycle,\n                 :cycle [\"ca\" \"cb\"]}]\n    (testing \"ca imports cb imports ca: refused naming both, least first,\n              whichever unit the set lists first\"\n      (is (= refusal\n             (publication/publish-units!\n               store (h/registry) stand-in-address\n               [(unit \"ca\" programs/ca-packet)\n                (unit \"cb\" programs/cb-packet)])))\n      (is (= refusal\n             (publication/publish-units!\n               store (h/registry) stand-in-address\n               [(unit \"cb\" programs/cb-packet)\n                (unit \"ca\" programs/ca-packet)]))))\n    (testing \"nothing was written\"\n      (is (empty? ((:entries-fn store)))))))\n\n\n(deftest an-unsupplied-import-is-refused-at-publication-test\n  (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)]\n    (is (= {:status :refused,\n            :reason :yang.python.antlr/unpublished-import,\n            :module \"k\",\n            :imported-by \"t\"}\n           (publication/publish-units! store (h/registry) stand-in-address\n                                       [(unit \"t\" programs/t-packet)])))\n    (is (empty? ((:entries-fn store))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The mesh world: a publisher, two plain peers, a reader\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private big\n  \"Every node's inbound bound: py's closure is replicated whole.\"\n  (* 512 1024 1024))\n\n\n(defn- peer-node\n  [net port]\n  (let [c (mesh/join! net port {::jing.dht/publish? true\n                                ::jing.dht/max-inbound-bytes big})]\n    {:composition c, :state (jing.dht/state c)}))\n\n\n(defn- node-at\n  \"A node at mesh `port` whose local store already holds `seed`\n   ({address bytes}): content it has, not content it publishes.\"\n  [net port peer-ports publish? seed]\n  (dht/join {:local (mem/create-content-mem seed),\n             :publish? publish?,\n             :peers (mapv (fn [p] {:host mesh/host, :port p}) peer-ports),\n             :bind! (mesh/seam net port),\n             :max-inbound-bytes big}))\n\n\n(defn- step-world\n  \"One reading: the publisher, the reader when there is one, then every\n   plain peer.\"\n  [w]\n  (let [now (:now w)\n        [pub pub-events] (dht/step (:pub w) now)\n        [reader] (when (:reader w) (dht/step (:reader w) now))]\n    (-> w\n        (assoc :pub pub\n               :reader reader\n               :peers (into {}\n                            (map (fn [[port {:keys [composition state]}]]\n                                   (mesh/tick! composition now)\n                                   [port {:composition composition,\n                                          :state (jing.dht/step state 256)}]))\n                            (:peers w))\n               :now (+ now 10))\n        (update :events into pub-events))))\n\n\n(defn- run-world\n  \"Step `w` until `(done? w)`; `:failure` names `cause` when `span` more\n   readings pass first.\"\n  [w span cause done?]\n  (let [limit (+ (:now w) span)]\n    (loop [w w]\n      (cond\n        (done? w) w\n        (> (:now w) limit) (assoc w :failure cause)\n        :else (recur (step-world w))))))\n\n\n(defn- published?\n  [manifest]\n  (fn [w]\n    (some #(and (= :published (::dht/event %)) (= manifest (:manifest %)))\n          (:events w))))\n\n\n(defn- index!\n  \"Publish the signed envelopes `signed` (`{:envelope :proof}`) as one\n   index transaction through `node` and announce it: its manifest.\"\n  [node signed]\n  (dht-test/publish-datoms!\n    node\n    (vec (map-indexed (fn [i s]\n                        {:db/id (+ datom/first-user-id i),\n                         :yin.module/envelope (:envelope s),\n                         :yin.module/proof (:proof s)})\n                      signed))))\n\n\n(defn- publish-index\n  \"Publish `signed` as an index through the publisher, run until it is\n   reported, and load it onto the reader: `[w manifest]`.\"\n  [w signed]\n  (let [m (index! (:pub w) signed)\n        w (run-world w 600000 (str \"the index \" m \" was not reported\")\n                     (published? m))\n        _ (is (nil? (:failure w)) (:failure w))\n        w (run-world (update w :reader dht/load-index m)\n                     600000 (str \"the index \" m \" did not load\")\n                     #(contains? #{:loaded :failed}\n                                 (:status (dht/load-status (:reader %) m))))]\n    (is (nil? (:failure w)) (:failure w))\n    (is (= :loaded (:status (dht/load-status (:reader w) m))))\n    [w m]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; A run over the DHT link source\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- py-output\n  \"The lines the Python runtime of `task` has printed, read off its\n   `py.rt/out` cell in py's module store: none when py has not run\n   `py/init!`, so no Python statement can have printed.\"\n  [task]\n  (let [ref (some #(get % 'py.rt/out) (vals (:module-stores task)))]\n    (mapv render/line (when ref (get-in task [:heap (:id ref) :value])))))\n\n\n(defn- guest-installs\n  \"The guest modules `task` has started an install child for: the\n   `pym.*` names it has linked or is installing, as strings (a name\n   compares by its text whatever symbol value a kernel's registry\n   holds).\"\n  [task]\n  (into (sorted-set)\n        (comp (map str)\n              (filter #(= \"pym.\" (subs % 0 (min 4 (count %))))))\n        (concat (map first (module/module-entries (:modules task)))\n                (keys (:installs task)))))\n\n\n(defn- observed\n  \"What `task` shows independently of its value: the lines it printed,\n   the guest modules it installed, and how many install children it ever\n   started (its origin counter, `py`'s included).\"\n  [task]\n  {:output (py-output task),\n   :guests (guest-installs task),\n   :children (or (:origins task) 0),\n   :admissions (into {}\n                     (keep (fn [[n entry]]\n                             (when (contains? (guest-installs task) (str n))\n                               [(str n) (:admission entry)])))\n                     (module/module-entries (:modules task)))})\n\n\n(defn- run-over-dht\n  \"The linked program of packet `pk` on `backend`, its link pair served\n   by the DHT source `src` from the world's reader, the world stepped\n   between rounds: `[w outcome response observation]`, the outcome\n   `[halted? blocked? output]` or `[:thrown message]`. `response` is the\n   first refused pair response when any exists, else the latest served\n   response. The observation is `observed` of the task the program ended\n   as -- for a thrown run, of the task the throwing run resumed, which\n   holds every step before the raise: a refused link raises at its resume,\n   before anything else runs.\n\n   Both interpreters are driven and retained across rounds\n   (yin.vm.linker.dht.md 7.5): the link server, over the admission state\n   minted beside the pair, and the source's in-process admission\n   interpreter, when the source composes one, which answers each\n   question the server asks. `between`, `(between w served)` of each\n   serve round's result once the world is stepped, answers the world:\n   the place of an interpreter outside the process.\"\n  ([w backend pk src] (run-over-dht w backend pk src (fn [w _] w)))\n  ([w backend pk src between]\n   (let [pair (link/make-pair)\n         adm (admission/make-state link/pair-capacity)\n         interp (when (:admission src)\n                  (admission/interpreter adm (:admission src)))\n         task ((get h/backends backend)\n               (lower/lower-packet pk {:prelude :linked})\n               (h/composition (h/registry) pair))\n         limit (+ (:now w) 1200000)\n         run (fn [task]\n               (try (vm/run task)\n                    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default) e\n                      {::thrown (ex-message e), ::resumed task})))]\n     (loop [w w\n            task (run task)\n            pair pair\n            adm adm\n            interp interp]\n       (let [response (or (some #(when (= :refused (:status %))\n                                   (dissoc % :yin.link/id :image))\n                                (mesh/values (:responses pair)))\n                          (dissoc (peek (mesh/values (:responses pair)))\n                                  :yin.link/id :image))]\n         (cond\n           (::thrown task)\n           [w [:thrown (::thrown task)] response (observed (::resumed task))]\n\n           (and (vm/blocked? task) (< (:now w) limit))\n           (let [{:keys [pair dht admission] :as served}\n                 (link/serve {:pair pair,\n                              :source src,\n                              :dht (:reader w),\n                              :admission adm})\n                 admitted (when interp\n                            (admission/serve\n                              {:interpreter interp,\n                               :policy (:admission src),\n                               :context (admission/context {})}\n                              link/serve-budget))\n                 w (between (step-world (assoc w :reader dht)) served)]\n             (recur w\n                    (run task)\n                    pair\n                    admission\n                    (if admitted (:interpreter admitted) interp)))\n\n           :else\n           [w\n            [(vm/halted? task) (vm/blocked? task)\n             (render/output (vm/value task))]\n            response\n            (observed task)]))))))\n\n\n(defn- source\n  \"The reader's DHT link source declaring the public keys `publics`, its\n   in-process admission interpreter trusting the principals of the\n   public keys `trusted` -- none in process when `trusted` is nil.\"\n  [publics trusted]\n  (link/composition\n    {:dht? true,\n     :principals publics,\n     :admission (when trusted\n                  {:trusted (set (map sign/principal trusted))})}))\n\n\n(defn- on-every-vm\n  \"Thread `w` through `run-over-dht` on every vector backend: `[w {backend\n   [outcome last-response observation]}]`.\"\n  [w pk src]\n  (reduce (fn [[w acc] k]\n            (let [[w outcome response seen] (run-over-dht w k pk src)]\n              [w (assoc acc k [outcome response seen])]))\n          [w {}]\n          (keys h/backends)))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The acceptance\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- first-difference\n  \"The first key of the artifacts `a` and `b` (`fixture/parse`'s data)\n   whose values differ, with the blob addresses only one holds or holds\n   other bytes at; nil when they are equal.\"\n  [a b]\n  (when (not= a b)\n    (let [blobs (fn [x y]\n                  (sort (map str (remove #(= (get x %) (get y %))\n                                         (keys x)))))]\n      {:keys (vec (sort (map str (filter #(not= (get a %) (get b %))\n                                         (distinct (concat (keys a)\n                                                           (keys b))))))),\n       :blobs-differ (vec (take 4 (blobs (:blobs a) (:blobs b)))),\n       :blobs-only-here (vec (take 4 (blobs (:blobs b) (:blobs a))))})))\n\n\n(defn- this-host-publishes-the-artifact\n  [artifact-lines]\n  (testing \"this host's own publication of the committed packets is the\n            JVM's artifact: same manifests, blobs and envelopes\"\n    (let [{:keys [lines refused]} (fixture/generate)]\n      (is (nil? refused) (pr-str refused))\n      (when lines\n        (is (nil? (first-difference (fixture/parse artifact-lines)\n                                    (fixture/parse lines))))))))\n\n\n(defn- publish-world\n  \"Publisher `A` at mesh port 1, plain peers at 2 and 3, a reader at 4,\n   `A` and the reader with `py` installed: `A`'s node serves the\n   artifact's guest blobs as they are and its first index (py, m, k and\n   t named by `A`), which the reader loads.\"\n  [artifact]\n  (let [net (mesh/mesh)\n        installed (fixture/installed-py)\n        pub (node-at net 1 [2 3] true installed)\n        put! (:put-bytes-fn (dht/store pub))\n        w {:net net,\n           :pub pub,\n           :reader (node-at net 4 [2 3 1] false installed),\n           :peers (into {} (map (fn [p] [p (peer-node net p)])) [2 3]),\n           :now 0,\n           :events []}]\n    (testing \"every node's installed py is the artifact's\"\n      (is (= (:py artifact) (:address @h/published))))\n    (run! (fn [[address bs]] (put! address bs))\n          (sort-by (comp str key) (:blobs artifact)))\n    (first (publish-index w (get-in artifact [:indexes :own])))))\n\n\n(def ^:private nothing-ran\n  \"A refused import's observation: no line printed and no guest install\n   child; the one child started is py's.\"\n  {:output [], :guests #{}, :children 1})\n\n\n(defn- observes\n  \"Assert each key of the observation `expected` of backend `k` on its\n   own, so a failure names the key.\"\n  [k expected seen]\n  (doseq [[key v] expected]\n    (is (= v (get seen key)) (str k \" \" key))))\n\n\n(defn- imports-over-the-dht\n  [w artifact src]\n  (testing \"a JVM-published pym.m imports over the DHT, parserless, with\n            the in-store linked run's output and CPython's\"\n    (let [[w results] (on-every-vm w (get-in artifact [:importers :d]) src)]\n      (doseq [[k [outcome response seen]] results]\n        (is (= [true false {:py/out [\"m-body\" \"7\"], :py/exception nil}]\n               outcome)\n            (str k \" \" (pr-str response)))\n        (testing \"and the observation sees the same run\"\n          (observes k {:output [\"m-body\" \"7\"], :guests #{\"pym.m\"},\n                       :children 2}\n                    seen)))\n      (testing \"and t delivers k, its pinned import, by name\"\n        (let [[w results] (on-every-vm w (get-in artifact [:importers :tt])\n                                       src)]\n          (doseq [[k [outcome response seen]] results]\n            (is (= [true false\n                    {:py/out [\"k-body\" \"t-sees 3\" \"t-done\"],\n                     :py/exception nil}]\n                   outcome)\n                (str k \" \" (pr-str response)))\n            (observes k {:guests #{\"pym.k\" \"pym.t\"}} seen))\n          w)))))\n\n\n(defn- republished-dependency-is-refused\n  [w artifact src]\n  (let [k1 (get-in artifact [:units \"k\"])\n        k2 (get-in artifact [:republished \"k\"])\n        [w _] (publish-index w (get-in artifact [:indexes :republish]))]\n    (testing \"a republished dependency: t pinned k's first address, k now\n              names another; the link server delivers k2, but the engine\n              refuses receive as a pin mismatch, raising ImportError in t\"\n      (is (not= k1 k2))\n      (let [[w results] (on-every-vm w (get-in artifact [:importers :tt])\n                                     src)]\n        (doseq [[k [outcome response seen]] results]\n          (is (= [true false\n                  {:py/out [],\n                   :py/exception\n                   {:type \"ImportError\",\n                    :args [\"Cannot import module 'k': linker refused delivery\"]}}]\n                 outcome)\n              (str k \" \" (pr-str outcome)))\n          (is (= {:status :ok,\n                  :yin.admit/address k2}\n                 (select-keys response [:status :yin.admit/address]))\n              (str k \" \" (pr-str response)))\n          (observes k {:output [], :guests #{\"pym.t\"}, :children 3} seen))\n        w))))\n\n\n;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n;; B's module: refused untrusted, allowed trusted, bound to its question\n;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n(def ^:private caught-e\n  \"x's run once e is linked: e.boom raises, x catches it.\"\n  [true false {:py/out [\"caught-e\"], :py/exception nil}])\n\n\n(defn- an-untrusted-principal-is-refused-on-every-vm\n  [w artifact]\n  (let [{:keys [a b]} (:principals artifact)\n        [w _] (publish-index w (get-in artifact [:indexes :foreign]))]\n    (testing \"a module only B vouches for, B declared and A alone trusted:\n              the default interpreter refuses it as untrusted, naming B,\n              raising ImportError in x before e installs\"\n      (let [[w results] (on-every-vm w (get-in artifact [:importers :x])\n                                     (source [a b] [a]))]\n        (doseq [[k [outcome response seen]] results]\n          (is (= [true false\n                  {:py/out [],\n                   :py/exception\n                   {:type \"ImportError\",\n                    :args [\"Cannot import module 'e': linker refused delivery\"]}}]\n                 outcome)\n              (str k \" \" (pr-str outcome)))\n          (is (= {:status :refused,\n                  :reason :yin.admit/untrusted-principal,\n                  :name 'pym.e,\n                  :yin.admit/decision :refuse,\n                  :yin.admit/asserters [(sign/principal b)]}\n                 (dissoc response :yin.admit/id))\n              (str k \" \" (pr-str response)))\n          (is (vector? (:yin.admit/id response)) (str k))\n          (observes k nothing-ran seen))\n        w))))\n\n\n(defn- a-trusted-principal-is-allowed-on-every-vm\n  [w artifact]\n  (let [{:keys [a b]} (:principals artifact)\n        e (get-in artifact [:units \"e\"])]\n    (testing \"the reader trusts B explicitly: e imports on every VM, its\n              registry entry recording the admission it rode on\"\n      (let [[w results] (on-every-vm w (get-in artifact [:importers :x])\n                                     (source [a b] [a b]))]\n        (doseq [[k [outcome response seen]] results]\n          (is (= caught-e outcome) (str k \" \" (pr-str response)))\n          (observes k {:output [\"caught-e\"],\n                       :guests #{\"pym.e\"},\n                       :children 2,\n                       :admissions {\"pym.e\"\n                                    {:yin.admit/id (:yin.admit/id response),\n                                     :yin.admit/decision :allow,\n                                     :yin.admit/asserters\n                                     [(sign/principal b)],\n                                     :yin.admit/address e}}}\n                    seen))\n        w))))\n\n\n(defn- install-confirmed\n  [follower node events]\n  (reduce (fn [[f n] e]\n            (if (= :confirmed (:yin.head/event e))\n              (let [[f n _] (head/install f n (:principal e) (:trace e))]\n                [f n])\n              [f n]))\n          [follower node]\n          events))\n\n\n(defn- follow-step\n  \"One reading of the world, then one pass of the reader's head\n   follower, installing what it confirms.\"\n  [w]\n  (let [w (step-world w)\n        [f node events] (head/step (:follower w) (:reader w) (:now w))\n        [f node] (install-confirmed f node events)]\n    (assoc w :follower f :reader node)))\n\n\n(defn- move-b-head\n  \"Publish B's next index through the publisher -- B's assertion of\n   pym.e retracted, pym.e now naming `m2` -- deposit its head on B's\n   board, and step the world and the reader's follower until the head is\n   installed: the world.\"\n  [w artifact m2]\n  (let [key-b fixture/key-b\n        pb (sign/principal (:public key-b))\n        [e1] (get-in artifact [:indexes :foreign])\n        signed [(publish/retraction\n                  key-b\n                  {:of (jing/segment-key (:envelope e1)), :seq 2})\n                (publish/assertion key-b\n                                   {:name 'pym.e, :manifest m2, :seq 3})]\n        m (index! (:pub w) signed)\n        w (run-world w 600000 (str \"B's head \" m \" was not reported\")\n                     (published? m))\n        dep (head/deposit! (:board w) key-b m\n                           (index/read-datoms (dht/local (:pub w)) m))\n        limit (+ (:now w) 600000)\n        w (loop [w w]\n            (cond\n              (= m (get (ld/installed-heads (:reader w)) pb)) w\n              (> (:now w) limit) (assoc w :failure \"B's head not installed\")\n              :else (recur (follow-step w))))]\n    (is (= :ok (:status dep)) (pr-str dep))\n    (is (nil? (:failure w)) (:failure w))\n    w))\n\n\n(defn- allow-after-the-head-moves\n  \"The `between` of `run-over-dht` for F1, an external interpreter: it\n   allows each question once, every name but pym.e at once (py is A's),\n   and pym.e only after moving B's head to `m2`. It records under\n   `:asked` every admission id a pending pym.e link names.\"\n  [artifact src m2]\n  (fn [w served]\n    (let [pending (filter :admission (:pending served))\n          e? #(= \"pym.e\" (str (:name %)))\n          w (update w :asked into (map :admission (filter e? pending)))\n          w (if (or (:moved w) (not-any? e? pending))\n              w\n              (let [w (move-b-head w artifact m2)]\n                (is (= m2 (:address (ld/resolve-name (:reader w)\n                                                     (link/authority src)\n                                                     'pym.e)))\n                    \"B's head moved pym.e to M2 while the question was open\")\n                (assoc w :moved true)))]\n      (reduce (fn [w {:keys [admission]}]\n                (if (contains? (:answered w) admission)\n                  w\n                  (do (stream/append! (get-in served\n                                              [:admission :pair :answers])\n                                      {:yin.admit/id admission,\n                                       :yin.admit/decision :allow,\n                                       :yin.admit/conditions {}})\n                      (update w :answered conj admission))))\n              w\n              pending))))\n\n\n(defn- an-allow-binds-the-address-the-question-was-asked-about\n  [w artifact]\n  (let [{:keys [a b]} (:principals artifact)\n        pb (sign/principal b)\n        m1 (get-in artifact [:units \"e\"])\n        m2 (get-in artifact [:republished \"k\"])\n        src (source [a b] nil)\n        [f reader] (head/follow (:reader w) {:follow [pb],\n                                             :heads :volatile,\n                                             :poll-ticks 10})\n        board (head/board)\n        w (assoc w\n                 :reader reader\n                 :follower (head/attach f pb board)\n                 :board board\n                 :asked #{}\n                 :answered #{})]\n    (testing \"M2 is a module the reader has never loaded\"\n      (is (not= m1 m2))\n      (is (nil? (ld/module-status (:reader w) m2))))\n    (testing \"an allow for the question about M1, answered after B's head\n              moved pym.e to M2, links M1 and never fetches M2 (F1)\"\n      (let [[w outcome response seen]\n            (run-over-dht w :semantic (get-in artifact [:importers :x]) src\n                          (allow-after-the-head-moves artifact src m2))\n            id (:yin.admit/id response)]\n        (is (:moved w) \"the question was asked and answered\")\n        (is (= caught-e outcome) (pr-str response))\n        (is (= m1 (:yin.admit/address response)))\n        (is (= (jing/get (dht/local (:pub w)) m1 nil) (:manifest response)))\n        (is (some? (ld/module-status (:reader w) m1)))\n        (is (nil? (ld/module-status (:reader w) m2)))\n        (is (= {\"pym.e\" {:yin.admit/id id,\n                         :yin.admit/decision :allow,\n                         :yin.admit/asserters [pb],\n                         :yin.admit/address m1}}\n               (:admissions seen)))\n        (is (= #{id} (:asked w)) \"the pending admission id never changed\")\n        w))))\n\n\n(defn- dht-import-test\n  []\n  (let [lines (fixture/read-lines)\n        _ (this-host-publishes-the-artifact lines)\n        artifact (fixture/read-file)\n        a (get-in artifact [:principals :a])\n        src (source [a] [a])\n        w (publish-world artifact)\n        w (imports-over-the-dht w artifact src)\n        w (an-untrusted-principal-is-refused-on-every-vm w artifact)\n        w (a-trusted-principal-is-allowed-on-every-vm w artifact)\n        w (an-allow-binds-the-address-the-question-was-asked-about\n            w artifact)\n        w (republished-dependency-is-refused w artifact src)]\n    (dht/close! (:pub w))\n    (dht/close! (:reader w))))\n\n\n(deftest ^:slow dht-import-test-test\n  (slow/guard \"dht-import-test\" dht-import-test))\nzsh:1: no matches found: src/dev/*dht*\n01a13b5c-d88c-7a01-a2f8-f409ef355091\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
