{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_109","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom zoneinfo import ZoneInfo\nimport os, subprocess\nnow=datetime.now(timezone.utc)\nthread=os.environ.get('CODEX_THREAD_ID')\nassert thread == '01a13b5c-d88c-7a01-a2f8-f409ef355091'\nheader=f\\\"Completed-GMT: {now.strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S GMT')}\\\\nCompleted-Local: {now.astimezone(ZoneInfo('Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh')).strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh')}\\\\nCoding-Agent: codex\\\\nSession-ID: {thread}\\\\n\\\"\nbody='''\nPhase-8ab fix round 2 completed in the named worktree. No commit was made.\n\n## Base and scope\n\n- Branch \"'`srvm-phase8ab`, HEAD `2b9f2b47c3b3aaaf1c2a7c23fcbe476e190dc6fd`.\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 72592bd9 HEAD`: exit 0 at start and finish.\n- `72592bd9` changes only the yang.python-owned EDN and DHT test over I4-a `d27adce4`; the branch'\"'s next commit is the rebased 8ab implementation.\n- Read master architecture rules, phase-8 plan §1.4, the supplied regen script, Fable review, fix-1 report, initial engineering report, yang.python reply, and build/test guide.\n- Session-ID captured from \"'`CODEX_THREAD_ID`; a dispatch `thread.started` event is not exposed to this turn.\n\n## Changed files and moved constants\n\n| File | Changes |\n|---|---|\n| `test/yang/python/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc` | py manifest pin, runtime-key count, manifest provenance docstring; 4 added / 3 deleted lines |\n| `test/yang/python/antlr/linked_safepoint_test.cljc` | pysp manifest pin and provenance docstring; 3 added / 2 deleted lines |\n| `collab/1792633000000-engineer-8ab-fix2.report.md` | This new worktree-local report |\n\n| Pin | Old prefix/value | New prefix/value |\n|---|---|---|\n| py manifest | `577aabfb8632` | `2e5aebac74d6` |\n| pysp manifest | `6c39c4b94a08` | `a28d246c0257` |\n| prelude runtime-key count | 65 | 66 |\n\nFull new addresses:\n\n- py: `:segment/blake3-2e5aebac74d6d39593fed020c333f1f5b42ae4128d4789a24f73dc88083cafc3`\n- pysp: `:segment/blake3-a28d246c025785ad24467a95df3c1da821897a323c2d9838e7bcd29cf5d88580`\n\nI4-a added `ModuleNotFoundError` to the builtin classes and changed statement-time import delivery. Its additional class accounts for runtime-keys moving from 65 to 66. The first quick run exposed this stale constant (250 tests, 8,483 assertions, 1 failure, 0 errors, exit 1); updating the exact count preserves the adjacent assertion that the generated initializer defines precisely those keys.\n\n## Re-derivation and unchanged pins\n\n`clojure -M collab/1792620000000-8ab-regen.clj` exited 0. All 51 saved-input outputs are byte-identical to `target/8ab/regen-2.edn` (`cmp`, exit 0), including the descriptor equality checks and exact handoff fixture wire-byte assertions.\n\nThe supplied script stores historical manifest maps in the companion intermediates EDN. Hashing those saved maps necessarily reproduces the pre-I4-a `577aabfb` / `6c39c4b9` values; that alone is not current-tree publication evidence. Therefore I separately published both current module specs via the public `linked-harness` publication values, read each complete manifest with `jing/get`, and asserted its address equals `jing/segment-key` of that map. That JVM probe exited 0 and produced the new addresses above. Full manifest inputs are saved in `target/8ab-fix2/py-manifest.edn` and `pysp-manifest.edn`; its stdout is `live-manifests.log`. The original supplied script and intermediates remain unchanged.\n\nAll 49 non-py/pysp saved regeneration entries stayed identical to the prior 8ab run. In particular:\n\n- H descriptor `7b7c6ae92e5f`, R descriptor `aa757659a28f`, dimension descriptor `4b69e00d1da9`.\n- All H/R backend image goldens, six dimension/node/projection goldens, old register compiler checksum pins, all 20 derive H/R pins, linker H `d07cb2e9a417` and R `bc06914564a0`, parity image hashes and wire bytes.\n- Handoff address `52c7efaa3967` and exact fixture bytes.\n- All 32 corpus A pins and 20 rows pins; corpus, rows, layout, surviving safepoint harness, `rows-checkpoint-v3.txt`, and `ledger-v2.txt` are byte-identical to HEAD.\n- Prelude-independent linked-program root `dbe72b291a26` remains unchanged and its slow assertion passed.\n\nFinal `git diff --quiet HEAD -- <all backend/golden/parity/linker/corpus/rows/fixture files plus both protected DHT files>` exited 0. No backend, descriptor, dimension/node, linker, parity, CESK, execution-parity, corpus or rows code/pins were changed by this fix. Existing untracked collab files were preserved.\n\n## JVM verification\n\n| Check | Outcome |\n|---|---|\n| Final kondo on both changed Clojure files | Exit 0; 0 errors, 0 warnings |\n| Focused quick after the count fix | Exit 0; 250 tests, 8,483 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors |\n| Focused quick again after all mutant restorations | Exit 0; 250 tests, 8,483 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors |\n| Focused slow plus DHT, committed EDN | Exit 1; 18 tests, 289 assertions, 66 failures, 0 errors; every failure in `dht-import-test-test` |\n| Local EDN generator | Exit 0; wrote artifact using committed packets and fixed fixture seeds |\n| DHT slow leg, locally regenerated EDN | Exit 0; 1 test, 92 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors |\n| Protected files and unchanged pin files comparison | Exit 0 |\n| `git diff --check` | Exit 0; clean |\n\nQuick command (both passing runs):\n\n```sh\nclojure -M:test -e :slow -n yin.vm.debruijn-test -n yin.vm.debruijn-code-test -n yin.vm.debruijn-register-code-test -n yin.vm.debruijn-register-compile-test -n yin.vm.debruijn.stack-parity-test -n yin.vm.linker-test -n yin.vm.semantic-register.derive-test -n yang.python.antlr.linked-prelude-test -n yang.python.antlr.linked-safepoint-test -n yin.vm.ucf.handoff-v2-census-test\n```\n\nCommitted-artifact slow command uses the same ten namespaces with `-i :slow`, adding `-n yang.python.antlr.dht-import-test`. No failures occurred outside DHT. C4 completed 10 root programs and 8 module bodies on both kernel families.\n\nLocal slow command:\n\n```sh\nclojure -M:test -i :slow -n yang.python.antlr.dht-import-test\n```\n\nLint command:\n\n```sh\nclj -M:kondo --lint test/yang/python/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc test/yang/python/antlr/linked_safepoint_test.cljc\n```\n\nNo ANTLR parser or loopback socket failure occurred, and no new environment workaround or source expansion was needed. Node and Dart were not run, as explicitly instructed.\n\n## Committed-artifact assertion deltas and EDN restoration\n\nThe expected-red DHT run found:\n\n- Line 382: publication comparison differs in `:blobs`, `:indexes`, `:py`, `:republished`, and `:units` (the exact diagnostic blob addresses are retained in `slow-committed.log`).\n- Line 403: committed py `6e003ac4ac8e` versus current-tree py `2e5aebac74d6`.\n- All downstream import paths attempt the committed py address, which is absent from the newly installed prelude store. Responses refuse with `:reason :absent`, the committed py address, and `:cause :dao.jing.dht/exhausted`; runs produce `[:thrown \"Module link refused: absent\"]`. Consequently expected module outputs, guest installs, child counts, admission data and follow-head behavior do not materialize.\n\nFailure counts by assertion line in `dht_import_test.cljc`:\n\n| Line | Failures |\n|---|---:|\n| 382, 403 | 1 each |\n| 420 | 33 |\n| 429, 440, 461, 468, 495, 502, 509, 523 | 3 each |\n| 645, 646, 647, 648, 649, 651, 656 | 1 each |\n\nThese total 66 failures. The locally regenerated artifact makes the complete DHT acceptance green (92 assertions). No test assertions were edited or weakened.\n\nThe generator command was the exact JVM command from the generator header:\n\n```sh\nclojure -Sdeps '\"'{:aliases {:t {:extra-paths [\\\"test\\\"]}}}' -M:t test/resources/yang/python/dht-import-v1.generate.clj\n\"'```\n\nThe temporary EDN was then restored with `git checkout -- test/resources/yang/python/dht-import-v1.edn`. The first sandboxed checkout exited 128 because the worktree index lock lives under the main repository'\"'s \"'`.git`, outside the writable root. The same explicitly authorized restore succeeded with approved filesystem access (exit 0). This was a restoration-access issue; generator and test exits were both 0. Final comparison to HEAD succeeded for the EDN and untouched `dht_import_test.cljc`.\n\nFinal EDN status command and actual output:\n\n```sh\ngit status --short -- test/resources/yang/python/dht-import-v1.edn\n```\n\nOutput: empty (no status line; EDN unmodified). Captured in `target/8ab-fix2/edn-status-final.log`. The temporary artifact and its diff are retained only as ignored evidence under `target/8ab-fix2/`.\n\n## Four prior mutants, no new mutants\n\nEach mutant was applied alone, its diff and original bytes saved, and its selected JVM test run exited 1. Each file was restored from its saved bytes in a finally block; byte equality and before/after Git diff equality were asserted. The final focused quick run passed after all four restorations.\n\n| Prior mutant | Selected test | Tests / assertions | Failures / errors |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| H `image-hash` left on `jing/sha256` | `yin.vm.debruijn-code-test/golden-corpus-bytes-and-hash` | 1 / 12 | 4 / 0 |\n| Register descriptor `:hash` row left `:sha256` | `yin.vm.debruijn-register-code-test/golden-descriptor-hash-test` | 1 / 1 | 1 / 0 |\n| `:const-long` H pin computed with SHA-256 over current descriptor/image encoding | `yin.vm.debruijn-code-test/golden-corpus-bytes-and-hash` | 1 / 12 | 1 / 0 |\n| Old worked-example H `52791d4a…` retained in new lowerer golden | `yin.vm.semantic-register.derive-test/stack-goldens` | 1 / 31 | 1 / 0 |\n\nAll commands were `clojure -M:test -v <selected-test>`. The wrong-algorithm value was independently recomputed on this tree with `(jing/sha256 (str dc/descriptor-hash (dc/encode-image [[:const 42] [:return]])))`: `779facf9eb1ef9b5fd8aef6d57033d11659a2e6af7676c034edeb1918659ad9b`, matching the prior mutant. Logs, diffs, backups and restore results are in `target/8ab-fix2/`.\n\n## Concerns and incomplete work\n\nNo unresolved implementation concern or incomplete work remains within this JVM-only fix scope. With the protected committed master EDN restored, the branch'\"'s DHT artifact acceptance remains expected-red until the yang.python-owned artifact is regenerated on the integrated tree. This expected mismatch is explicitly authorized by the brief and was proved green with local regeneration. Cross-host verification and artifact landing remain outside this task; no claim is made about those gates.\n'''\np=Path('collab/1792633000000-engineer-8ab-fix2.report.md')\np.write_text(header+body)\nprint(header)\nprint('Report written:',p)\nPY\ngit diff --check; git status --short -- test/resources/yang/python/dht-import-v1.edn test/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc; git diff --stat\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
